{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HY15wrmqFYNqW2YTcA5ixy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — contamcal-irt-calibration\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- **Primary: EMNLP 2026 ARR May 25** (D006: reinstated per user directive, 12 days)\n5\t- Fallback: AAAI 2027 (Jul-Aug 2026) / ICLR 2027 (Sep 2026)\n6\t- Track: Machine Learning for NLP / Resources and Evaluation\n7\t- Aligns with EMNLP 2026 special theme \"New Missions for NLP Research\" (explicitly invites contamination/data governance work)\n8\t\n9\t## Core Insight\n10\tWhen benchmark mitigation strategies systematically fail (Emperor's New Clothes, ICML 2025: 20 strategies tested, none effective), the principled alternative is post-hoc statistical calibration — analogous to causal inference's shift from eliminating confounders to statistically controlling them. ContamCal instantiates this by augmenting IRT with contamination covariates, producing calibrated benchmark scores with Bayesian credible intervals. Theoretically grounded in educational measurement's item compromise IRT tradition (Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017) and explanatory IRT (De Boeck & Wilson 2004), with 3 non-trivial adaptations for LLM evaluation.\n11\t\n12\t## Core Claims (3 条)\n13\t\n14\t1. **Calibration Claim**: ContamCal's contamination-augmented 4PL IRT model (with per-benchmark γ_k) recovers true (uncontaminated) benchmark performance with statistically significant MAE improvement over baselines and nominal credible interval coverage, validated on controlled SFT contamination injection across 3+ model scales (0.5B-7B) within the Qwen2.5 family and 4 benchmarks. (Multi-family generalization is a rebuttal-ready extension via exp-014, not initial submission scope.)\n15\t\n16\t2. **Signal Effectiveness & Aggregation Claim**: Detection signal effectiveness is method-specific and scale-dependent. Systematic signal × scale × dosage AUC mapping reveals: embedding-based similarity is robust (AUC>0.95 at d005/0.5B), while Min-K++ and Self-Critique fail at small model scales (AUC≈0.5 at 0.5B). Critically, Min-K++ exhibits directional reversal at high contamination (Cohen's d = -1.2 to -2.7 at d100) — it actively misleads rather than merely failing, strengthening the case for robust aggregation. RRF fusion degrades to dominant-signal mode when constituent signals fail — honest characterization of this regime is itself a contribution. Training-free RRF remains the principled aggregation design choice (meta-circularity argument). Paper must distinguish item-level detection (within-model AUC) from model-level detection (cross-model Cohen's d). (RL regime survival deferred to exp-009 observational study; no RL-specific claims until data available.)\n17\t   **C2 contingency (Reviewer WARNING)**: \"Scale-dependent\" is currently unverified — only 0.5B data exists. If 1.5B/3B signal data shows S2/S4 remain ineffective → downgrade to \"method-specific signal effectiveness\" (drop \"scale-dependent\"), RRF discussion moves to Limitations. Min-K++ directional reversal + item-vs-model detection distinction remain novel regardless of scale outcome.\n18\t\n19\t3. **Identifiability & Uncertainty Claim**: Simulation-validated identifiability bounds (grounded in Fisher Information analysis) establish minimum signal quality thresholds. ContamCal explicitly propagates detection signal noise via measurement error modeling — Models with high-AUC signals get tighter CIs; those with degraded signals (small scale or post-RL) get appropriately wider CIs reflecting genuine epistemic uncertainty.\n20\t\n21\t## Contributions (Hierarchical — D025 rebalanced per Dream full-mode)\n22\t\n23\t### Core (co-equal; if calibration numbers weak, lean on #2 and #3)\n24\t1. ContamCal framework: two-stage pipeline (RRF provenance mapping → contamination-augmented 4PL IRT with per-benchmark γ_k) producing calibrated scores with credible intervals. ME model: report if it improves coverage; otherwise present simple model as primary and ME as ablation (D025/D8 — must clarify which model produced reported results)\n25\t2. Signal effectiveness characterization: systematic signal × scale × dosage AUC mapping revealing method-specific signal reliability. Min-K++ directional reversal (Cohen's d = -1.2 to -2.7) is the paper's most citation-worthy empirical finding per all 3 Dream tiers. Per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity (cross-family r=0.91 if confirmed) suggests contamination susceptibility is a benchmark property\n26\t3. Fisher Information identifiability analysis: structural (AUC≥0.55) vs practical (AUC≥0.70/0.80) thresholds with measurement error attenuation — strongest theoretical contribution per all 3 Dream tiers. Elevated from Supporting (D025)\n27\t\n28\t### Supporting\n29\t4. Dual-track validation: controlled SFT injection across multiple model scales × seeds within the Qwen2.5 family (internal validity) + ecological RL case study (external validity)\n30\t5. 7 baselines + 6 quantitative evaluation metrics (incl. SBC diagnostic per D025) + bootstrap CIs for contamination-aware calibration methodology\n31\t\n32\t## Story Spine\n33\t- **Problem**: Benchmark scores are increasingly unreliable due to training data contamination. Rephrased test items inflate MMLU accuracy by 8-15 points while evading n-gram decontamination. RL post-training may further complicate detection (under investigation, exp-009). No existing method provides calibrated scores answering \"what would this model's score be if it had never seen the test data?\"\n34\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Detection methods (Min-K%++, ConStat, Self-Critique, KDS) flag contamination but don't calibrate scores. IRT methods (PSN-IRT, Growing Pains, ATLAS, Lalor et al. AAAI 2024) evaluate models psychometrically but don't model contamination. DCR provides adjusted accuracy but lacks uncertainty bounds and RL handling. HiBayES provides Bayesian uncertainty but ignores contamination. Emperor's New Clothes (ICML 2025) demonstrates that all 20 mitigation strategies fail — motivating post-hoc calibration. Dynamic benchmarks (LiveBench) offer an alternative but require continuous curation.\n35\t- **Our framing**: ContamCal is a \"statistical safety net\" for when mitigation is unreliable. Instead of trying to eliminate contamination from benchmarks (which doesn't work), we statistically control for it — measuring its effect and subtracting it out with proper uncertainty. Grounded in educational measurement's item compromise IRT (Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017) and explanatory IRT (De Boeck & Wilson 2004), with 3 non-trivial structural adaptations: (a) independent examinees → single model with joint item distribution (changes local independence semantics — see §Local Independence below), (b) binary leakage → continuous exposure scores (standard technique in explanatory IRT; our contribution is the noise propagation pipeline, not the continuous covariate itself — D025 clarification per Dream R2), (c) stable ability → regime-conditional ability (different training regimes and model scales require method-aware, scale-aware signal selection).\n36\t- **Headline result template**: \"On {benchmark}, ContamCal recovers true model performance within {X}pp MAE (bootstrap 95% CI: [{lo}, {hi}]) with {Y}% credible interval coverage, while naive scores overestimate by {Z} points under {W}% contamination dosage.\"\n37\t\n38\t## Venue Fit Risks\n39\t- **EMNLP (primary)**: Best venue fit — special theme explicitly invites contamination/data governance. Reviewers deeply familiar with NLP contamination literature (advantage: no need to motivate the problem heavily). Risk: reviewers may be less familiar with IRT/psychometric methods (mitigation: add intuitive explanations, visual pipeline overview, and connection to familiar NLP concepts like calibration/confidence estimation). Risk: may expect broader model coverage beyond Qwen2.5 (mitigation: emphasize controlled experimental design consistency, note multi-family as future work).\n40\t- **AAAI/ICLR (fallback)**: Strong fit for Bayesian/probabilistic methods. Reviewers may need more contamination context but appreciate methodological rigor.\n41\t- **Novelty positioning**: Core method is cross-disciplinary synthesis (detection signals + explanatory IRT + measurement error). NOT positioned as \"new algorithm\" — positioned as (a) signal effectiveness characterization as empirically novel finding, (b) identifiability bounds with theoretical grounding, (c) first framework bridging detection → calibration with proper UQ. RRF is a principled design choice (meta-circularity argument), not claimed as methodological contribution.\n42\t- **RL limitation**: RL models get wide CIs. This is honest — frame as \"calibration is only as good as its inputs.\" Expected regret quantification uses held-out clean benchmark as ground truth (NOT calibrated scores, to avoid circularity).\n43\t\n44\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Defenses\n45\t\n46\t| # | Concern | Defense | Experiment |\n47\t|---|---------|---------|------------|\n48\t| 1 | θ and γ identifiable? | Fisher Information analysis + 144-condition simulation sweep + MVP validation | exp-004 |\n49\t| 2 | Why not learned aggregation? | Meta-circularity: learned aggregator's training data may itself be contaminated; RRF is design choice, not contribution | exp-003 |\n50\t| 3 | SFT injection ≠ real contamination | Dual-track: controlled SFT (internal) + ecological RL (external) + near-zero γ check (specificity). SFT is \"best-available proxy\", acknowledged as limitation | exp-006, exp-009 |\n51\t| 4 | Scale limited to 3B | 7B controlled + 72B observational | exp-007, exp-012 |\n52\t| 5 | Why 4PL not 2PL? | MVP: 2PL γ=0.16 vs 4PL γ=0.34 at N=100; c/d necessary for realistic item modeling | exp-006 |\n53\t| 6 | Too few models (N≈15)? | D025 multi-seed strategy: 3 scales × 4+ dosages × 2-3 seeds = 24-36 models pooled. Target N≥30 minimum (N≥50 ideal). Simulation sweep (exp-004) establishes identifiability at actual N. Growing Pains pre-estimation as backup at very low N | exp-004, exp-001 |\n54\t| 7 | Noisy exposure scores | Measurement error model (exposure as noisy observation of latent τ) propagates uncertainty into posteriors automatically | exp-005 |\n55\t| 8 | No baselines | 7 baselines including DCR (EMNLP 2025) + bootstrap CIs on all comparisons | exp-006 |\n56\t| 9 | Single global γ misspecified? | Per-benchmark γ_k is primary (natural in per-benchmark fitting); joint model with shared global γ is ablation. Report both to show contamination effect heterogeneity across benchmarks | exp-006 |\n57\t| 10 | Local independence violated? | Discussed explicitly; single model responds to all items → item responses correlated through shared parameters. Empirically test via posterior predictive checks on item-level residual correlations. This is a known IRT limitation when N_examinees is small. | exp-006 |\n58\t| 11 | Single model family? | Acknowledged as limitation. Qwen2.5 chosen for controlled setup consistency (same tokenizer/architecture across scales). Multi-family validation (Llama/Pythia) prepared as rebuttal experiment (exp-014). | exp-014 (rebuttal) |\n59\t| 12 | RL regret circular? | Ground truth for regret = held-out clean benchmark scores, NOT calibrated scores. Explicitly stated | exp-009 |\n60\t| 13 | S2/S4 fail at 0.5B — RRF is just S1? | Scale-dependent: honestly report single-signal regime at 0.5B. Verify S2/S4 at 1.5B/3B. RRF value = principled aggregation when signals ARE available + graceful degradation when not. | exp-008, exp-002 |\n61\t| 14 | d100 AUC=0.5 as signal failure? | Labeling artifact: d100 contaminates ALL items → labels lose discriminative power. Must NOT be interpreted as signal degradation. Present only d005/d025 for signal evaluation. | exp-008 |\n62\t| 15 | Novelty ceiling — standard IRT synthesis? (D025, all 3 Dream tiers) | Positioned as cross-disciplinary synthesis, NOT new algorithm. Emergent value: (a) per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity as benchmark property, (b) Min-K++ reversal as cautionary finding, (c) Fisher Info identifiability boundaries. If 4PL vs 2PL gap small → acknowledge honestly but argue c/d params needed for realistic MC modeling. Report oracle-γ ablation to decompose MAE. | exp-006 |\n63\t| 16 | Per-benchmark γ_k via separate fits, not hierarchical? (D025, [M][W]) | Per-benchmark separate fits = primary (natural, avoids cross-benchmark correlation). Hierarchical γ_k ~ Normal(μ_γ, σ_γ) as ablation to formally test heterogeneity and share info across benchmarks. Both reported. | exp-006 |\n64\t| 17 | Coverage gap — 85% vs 95% nominal? (D025, all 3 tiers) | SBC diagnostic to identify source. Possible causes: local independence violation, insufficient N, model misspecification. Report SBC alongside posterior predictive checks. If gap is from local independence → discuss as known IRT limitation with references. | exp-004, exp-006 |\n65\t| 18 | Why not just S1 alone? (D025, [M][W]) | S1-only is a baseline (#2 single-signal 2PL+γ). If RRF ≤ S1-only → present as \"S1+IRT calibration with extensible multi-signal architecture for future signals.\" Meta-circularity argument for training-free aggregation still holds. | exp-003 |\n66\t\n67\t## Evaluation Protocol (6 Metrics — D025 added SBC)\n68\t1. **Calibration error**: MAE between calibrated score and ground-truth clean accuracy, with bootstrap 95% CIs\n69\t2. **Interval coverage**: Fraction of true values within 50%/80%/95% credible intervals\n70\t3. **Interval sharpness**: Average CI width (tighter is better at fixed coverage)\n71\t4. **Ranking preservation**: Kendall's τ between calibrated and ground-truth model rankings\n72\t5. **Dose-response monotonicity**: γ effect increases monotonically with contamination dosage\n73\t6. **SBC diagnostic** (D025): Simulation-Based Calibration (Talts et al. 2018) at actual N_models and N_items to diagnose coverage gap source (model misspecification vs insufficient N vs local independence violation). CPU-only, parallelize with GPU experiments\n74\t\n75\t## Benchmarks (2 main + 2 contrasts)\n76\t1. **MMLU** — knowledge-intensive multiple-choice (14K items, subsampled 1000 for NUTS) — PRIMARY\n77\t2. **ARC-Challenge** — science reasoning multiple-choice (~1.2K items) — PRIMARY\n78\t3. **GSM8K** — mathematical reasoning free-form (~1.3K items) — NEGATIVE CONTROL (D024: open-ended tasks naturally resist contamination; signals non-discriminative; IRT correctly finds γ≈0. Paper frames as \"ContamCal identifies benchmarks not requiring calibration\")\n79\t4. **HumanEval** (appendix only) — code generation (N=164). Demoted D009: paraphrase QC 16%.\n80\t\n81\t## Baselines (7)\n82\t0. **Raw (no adjustment)** — report original benchmark scores as anchor\n83\t1. **Remove-and-rescore** — drop flagged items, rescore on remaining\n84\t2. **Single-signal 2PL+γ** — best single detection signal + simpler IRT\n85\t3. **Vanilla 4PL** — standard IRT without contamination covariate (γ=0)\n86\t4. **Linear exposure regression + bootstrap CI** — simplest post-hoc adjustment (tests if IRT complexity is necessary)\n87\t5. **Emperor's mitigation strategies** — rephrasing + option shuffling (2 representative strategies from ICML 2025)\n88\t6. **DCR fuzzy inference (EMNLP 2025)** — the only existing method producing adjusted accuracy; direct predecessor, must compare\n89\t\n90\t## Local Independence Discussion\n91\tStandard IRT assumes independent examinees. In LLM evaluation, a single model produces all item responses — responses are correlated through shared model parameters. This fundamentally alters local independence. Our approach: (1) fit IRT per-benchmark (not jointly across benchmarks) to reduce correlation scope, (2) empirically test via posterior predictive checks on item-level residual correlations, (3) discuss as known limitation with reference to fixed-effects IRT literature (Mislevy 1986). The coverage gap (if observed) may partly reflect this violation — measurement error model for exposure partially compensates by widening CIs.\n92\t\n93\t## Required Figures (Dream D2: \"zero figures\" flagged as serious deficiency)\n94\t1. Pipeline overview diagram (2-stage: RRF → 4PL+γ IRT)\n95\t2. Signal × scale × dosage AUC heatmap (exp-008) — 'regime' axis replaced by scale+dosage per D022\n96\t3. Dose-response curves (contamination dosage vs accuracy inflation, exp-001/006)\n97\t4. Identifiability phase diagram (AUC × N_models → γ recoverability, exp-004)\n98\t5. Calibrated-vs-true accuracy scatter with CIs (exp-006)\n99\t\n100\t## Citation Requirements (35+ minimum, expanded per Dream D2)\n101\tMust include: Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017, De Boeck & Wilson 2004, Adams et al. 1997, San Martín et al. 2009, Maris & Bechger 2009, Cormack et al. 2009 (RRF), Mislevy 1986, Lalor et al. AAAI 2024, LiveBench, TinyBenchmarks (Polo et al. 2024), KDS, CDD, contamination surveys, SBC (Talts et al. 2018), HiBayES, plus all signals/methods cited in IDEA_BRIEF.\n102\tDream D2 additions (all 3 tiers flagged):\n103\t- DIF literature: Holland & Wainer 1993, Thissen et al. 1993, Zumbo 1999 (γ_k is essentially DIF between exposure groups)\n104\t- ML calibration: Guo et al. 2017, Platt 1999 (disambiguate \"calibration\" — ours is decontamination, not probability calibration)\n105\t- Conformal prediction: Angelopoulos & Bates 2023 (alternative UQ with distribution-free coverage guarantees; discuss why Bayesian IRT preferred)\n106\t- Data attribution: Pruthi et al. 2020 (TracIn), Park et al. 2023 (TRAK) — potential additional signals, mention in Future Work\n107\t- Multidimensional IRT: Reckase 2009 (acknowledge unidimensional θ for MMLU as simplification in Limitations)\n108\tD025 additions (all 3 Dream tiers flagged):\n109\t- MIA foundations: Shokri et al. 2017 (membership inference attacks), Carlini et al. 2022 (extracting training data) — contextualize Min-K++ reversal in MIA literature\n110\t- Alternative evaluation: HELM (Liang et al. 2023), Chatbot Arena (Zheng et al. 2023) — discuss in Related Work as contamination-bypassing alternatives\n111\t- Deeper DCR engagement: Oren et al. 2024 structural comparison\n112\t- Burnell et al. 2023: multidimensional IRT for LLMs (relevant to unidimensional θ limitation)\n113\t\n114\t## Fisher Information Derivation (Dream D2: all 3 tiers flagged as critical gap)\n115\tMust derive I(γ) for 4PL+γ model in appendix. Currently stated without proof.\n116\tThe derivation must show: (1) relationship between signal AUC and γ recoverability, (2) approximation assumptions, (3) how measurement error factors in.\n117\tThis is CPU-only theoretical work — can be done in parallel with GPU experiments.\n118\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f90ec4b5-4e3f-4b38-a708-c8452c5be663","uuid":"d388b326-37d0-439a-94f9-53b4f0a28d91","timestamp":"2026-05-14T19:37:53.538Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T185145/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — contamcal-irt-calibration\n\n## Target Venue\n- **Primary: EMNLP 2026 ARR May 25** (D006: reinstated per user directive, 12 days)\n- Fallback: AAAI 2027 (Jul-Aug 2026) / ICLR 2027 (Sep 2026)\n- Track: Machine Learning for NLP / Resources and Evaluation\n- Aligns with EMNLP 2026 special theme \"New Missions for NLP Research\" (explicitly invites contamination/data governance work)\n\n## Core Insight\nWhen benchmark mitigation strategies systematically fail (Emperor's New Clothes, ICML 2025: 20 strategies tested, none effective), the principled alternative is post-hoc statistical calibration — analogous to causal inference's shift from eliminating confounders to statistically controlling them. ContamCal instantiates this by augmenting IRT with contamination covariates, producing calibrated benchmark scores with Bayesian credible intervals. Theoretically grounded in educational measurement's item compromise IRT tradition (Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017) and explanatory IRT (De Boeck & Wilson 2004), with 3 non-trivial adaptations for LLM evaluation.\n\n## Core Claims (3 条)\n\n1. **Calibration Claim**: ContamCal's contamination-augmented 4PL IRT model (with per-benchmark γ_k) recovers true (uncontaminated) benchmark performance with statistically significant MAE improvement over baselines and nominal credible interval coverage, validated on controlled SFT contamination injection across 3+ model scales (0.5B-7B) within the Qwen2.5 family and 4 benchmarks. (Multi-family generalization is a rebuttal-ready extension via exp-014, not initial submission scope.)\n\n2. **Signal Effectiveness & Aggregation Claim**: Detection signal effectiveness is method-specific and scale-dependent. Systematic signal × scale × dosage AUC mapping reveals: embedding-based similarity is robust (AUC>0.95 at d005/0.5B), while Min-K++ and Self-Critique fail at small model scales (AUC≈0.5 at 0.5B). Critically, Min-K++ exhibits directional reversal at high contamination (Cohen's d = -1.2 to -2.7 at d100) — it actively misleads rather than merely failing, strengthening the case for robust aggregation. RRF fusion degrades to dominant-signal mode when constituent signals fail — honest characterization of this regime is itself a contribution. Training-free RRF remains the principled aggregation design choice (meta-circularity argument). Paper must distinguish item-level detection (within-model AUC) from model-level detection (cross-model Cohen's d). (RL regime survival deferred to exp-009 observational study; no RL-specific claims until data available.)\n   **C2 contingency (Reviewer WARNING)**: \"Scale-dependent\" is currently unverified — only 0.5B data exists. If 1.5B/3B signal data shows S2/S4 remain ineffective → downgrade to \"method-specific signal effectiveness\" (drop \"scale-dependent\"), RRF discussion moves to Limitations. Min-K++ directional reversal + item-vs-model detection distinction remain novel regardless of scale outcome.\n\n3. **Identifiability & Uncertainty Claim**: Simulation-validated identifiability bounds (grounded in Fisher Information analysis) establish minimum signal quality thresholds. ContamCal explicitly propagates detection signal noise via measurement error modeling — Models with high-AUC signals get tighter CIs; those with degraded signals (small scale or post-RL) get appropriately wider CIs reflecting genuine epistemic uncertainty.\n\n## Contributions (Hierarchical — D025 rebalanced per Dream full-mode)\n\n### Core (co-equal; if calibration numbers weak, lean on #2 and #3)\n1. ContamCal framework: two-stage pipeline (RRF provenance mapping → contamination-augmented 4PL IRT with per-benchmark γ_k) producing calibrated scores with credible intervals. ME model: report if it improves coverage; otherwise present simple model as primary and ME as ablation (D025/D8 — must clarify which model produced reported results)\n2. Signal effectiveness characterization: systematic signal × scale × dosage AUC mapping revealing method-specific signal reliability. Min-K++ directional reversal (Cohen's d = -1.2 to -2.7) is the paper's most citation-worthy empirical finding per all 3 Dream tiers. Per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity (cross-family r=0.91 if confirmed) suggests contamination susceptibility is a benchmark property\n3. Fisher Information identifiability analysis: structural (AUC≥0.55) vs practical (AUC≥0.70/0.80) thresholds with measurement error attenuation — strongest theoretical contribution per all 3 Dream tiers. Elevated from Supporting (D025)\n\n### Supporting\n4. Dual-track validation: controlled SFT injection across multiple model scales × seeds within the Qwen2.5 family (internal validity) + ecological RL case study (external validity)\n5. 7 baselines + 6 quantitative evaluation metrics (incl. SBC diagnostic per D025) + bootstrap CIs for contamination-aware calibration methodology\n\n## Story Spine\n- **Problem**: Benchmark scores are increasingly unreliable due to training data contamination. Rephrased test items inflate MMLU accuracy by 8-15 points while evading n-gram decontamination. RL post-training may further complicate detection (under investigation, exp-009). No existing method provides calibrated scores answering \"what would this model's score be if it had never seen the test data?\"\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Detection methods (Min-K%++, ConStat, Self-Critique, KDS) flag contamination but don't calibrate scores. IRT methods (PSN-IRT, Growing Pains, ATLAS, Lalor et al. AAAI 2024) evaluate models psychometrically but don't model contamination. DCR provides adjusted accuracy but lacks uncertainty bounds and RL handling. HiBayES provides Bayesian uncertainty but ignores contamination. Emperor's New Clothes (ICML 2025) demonstrates that all 20 mitigation strategies fail — motivating post-hoc calibration. Dynamic benchmarks (LiveBench) offer an alternative but require continuous curation.\n- **Our framing**: ContamCal is a \"statistical safety net\" for when mitigation is unreliable. Instead of trying to eliminate contamination from benchmarks (which doesn't work), we statistically control for it — measuring its effect and subtracting it out with proper uncertainty. Grounded in educational measurement's item compromise IRT (Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017) and explanatory IRT (De Boeck & Wilson 2004), with 3 non-trivial structural adaptations: (a) independent examinees → single model with joint item distribution (changes local independence semantics — see §Local Independence below), (b) binary leakage → continuous exposure scores (standard technique in explanatory IRT; our contribution is the noise propagation pipeline, not the continuous covariate itself — D025 clarification per Dream R2), (c) stable ability → regime-conditional ability (different training regimes and model scales require method-aware, scale-aware signal selection).\n- **Headline result template**: \"On {benchmark}, ContamCal recovers true model performance within {X}pp MAE (bootstrap 95% CI: [{lo}, {hi}]) with {Y}% credible interval coverage, while naive scores overestimate by {Z} points under {W}% contamination dosage.\"\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n- **EMNLP (primary)**: Best venue fit — special theme explicitly invites contamination/data governance. Reviewers deeply familiar with NLP contamination literature (advantage: no need to motivate the problem heavily). Risk: reviewers may be less familiar with IRT/psychometric methods (mitigation: add intuitive explanations, visual pipeline overview, and connection to familiar NLP concepts like calibration/confidence estimation). Risk: may expect broader model coverage beyond Qwen2.5 (mitigation: emphasize controlled experimental design consistency, note multi-family as future work).\n- **AAAI/ICLR (fallback)**: Strong fit for Bayesian/probabilistic methods. Reviewers may need more contamination context but appreciate methodological rigor.\n- **Novelty positioning**: Core method is cross-disciplinary synthesis (detection signals + explanatory IRT + measurement error). NOT positioned as \"new algorithm\" — positioned as (a) signal effectiveness characterization as empirically novel finding, (b) identifiability bounds with theoretical grounding, (c) first framework bridging detection → calibration with proper UQ. RRF is a principled design choice (meta-circularity argument), not claimed as methodological contribution.\n- **RL limitation**: RL models get wide CIs. This is honest — frame as \"calibration is only as good as its inputs.\" Expected regret quantification uses held-out clean benchmark as ground truth (NOT calibrated scores, to avoid circularity).\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Defenses\n\n| # | Concern | Defense | Experiment |\n|---|---------|---------|------------|\n| 1 | θ and γ identifiable? | Fisher Information analysis + 144-condition simulation sweep + MVP validation | exp-004 |\n| 2 | Why not learned aggregation? | Meta-circularity: learned aggregator's training data may itself be contaminated; RRF is design choice, not contribution | exp-003 |\n| 3 | SFT injection ≠ real contamination | Dual-track: controlled SFT (internal) + ecological RL (external) + near-zero γ check (specificity). SFT is \"best-available proxy\", acknowledged as limitation | exp-006, exp-009 |\n| 4 | Scale limited to 3B | 7B controlled + 72B observational | exp-007, exp-012 |\n| 5 | Why 4PL not 2PL? | MVP: 2PL γ=0.16 vs 4PL γ=0.34 at N=100; c/d necessary for realistic item modeling | exp-006 |\n| 6 | Too few models (N≈15)? | D025 multi-seed strategy: 3 scales × 4+ dosages × 2-3 seeds = 24-36 models pooled. Target N≥30 minimum (N≥50 ideal). Simulation sweep (exp-004) establishes identifiability at actual N. Growing Pains pre-estimation as backup at very low N | exp-004, exp-001 |\n| 7 | Noisy exposure scores | Measurement error model (exposure as noisy observation of latent τ) propagates uncertainty into posteriors automatically | exp-005 |\n| 8 | No baselines | 7 baselines including DCR (EMNLP 2025) + bootstrap CIs on all comparisons | exp-006 |\n| 9 | Single global γ misspecified? | Per-benchmark γ_k is primary (natural in per-benchmark fitting); joint model with shared global γ is ablation. Report both to show contamination effect heterogeneity across benchmarks | exp-006 |\n| 10 | Local independence violated? | Discussed explicitly; single model responds to all items → item responses correlated through shared parameters. Empirically test via posterior predictive checks on item-level residual correlations. This is a known IRT limitation when N_examinees is small. | exp-006 |\n| 11 | Single model family? | Acknowledged as limitation. Qwen2.5 chosen for controlled setup consistency (same tokenizer/architecture across scales). Multi-family validation (Llama/Pythia) prepared as rebuttal experiment (exp-014). | exp-014 (rebuttal) |\n| 12 | RL regret circular? | Ground truth for regret = held-out clean benchmark scores, NOT calibrated scores. Explicitly stated | exp-009 |\n| 13 | S2/S4 fail at 0.5B — RRF is just S1? | Scale-dependent: honestly report single-signal regime at 0.5B. Verify S2/S4 at 1.5B/3B. RRF value = principled aggregation when signals ARE available + graceful degradation when not. | exp-008, exp-002 |\n| 14 | d100 AUC=0.5 as signal failure? | Labeling artifact: d100 contaminates ALL items → labels lose discriminative power. Must NOT be interpreted as signal degradation. Present only d005/d025 for signal evaluation. | exp-008 |\n| 15 | Novelty ceiling — standard IRT synthesis? (D025, all 3 Dream tiers) | Positioned as cross-disciplinary synthesis, NOT new algorithm. Emergent value: (a) per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity as benchmark property, (b) Min-K++ reversal as cautionary finding, (c) Fisher Info identifiability boundaries. If 4PL vs 2PL gap small → acknowledge honestly but argue c/d params needed for realistic MC modeling. Report oracle-γ ablation to decompose MAE. | exp-006 |\n| 16 | Per-benchmark γ_k via separate fits, not hierarchical? (D025, [M][W]) | Per-benchmark separate fits = primary (natural, avoids cross-benchmark correlation). Hierarchical γ_k ~ Normal(μ_γ, σ_γ) as ablation to formally test heterogeneity and share info across benchmarks. Both reported. | exp-006 |\n| 17 | Coverage gap — 85% vs 95% nominal? (D025, all 3 tiers) | SBC diagnostic to identify source. Possible causes: local independence violation, insufficient N, model misspecification. Report SBC alongside posterior predictive checks. If gap is from local independence → discuss as known IRT limitation with references. | exp-004, exp-006 |\n| 18 | Why not just S1 alone? (D025, [M][W]) | S1-only is a baseline (#2 single-signal 2PL+γ). If RRF ≤ S1-only → present as \"S1+IRT calibration with extensible multi-signal architecture for future signals.\" Meta-circularity argument for training-free aggregation still holds. | exp-003 |\n\n## Evaluation Protocol (6 Metrics — D025 added SBC)\n1. **Calibration error**: MAE between calibrated score and ground-truth clean accuracy, with bootstrap 95% CIs\n2. **Interval coverage**: Fraction of true values within 50%/80%/95% credible intervals\n3. **Interval sharpness**: Average CI width (tighter is better at fixed coverage)\n4. **Ranking preservation**: Kendall's τ between calibrated and ground-truth model rankings\n5. **Dose-response monotonicity**: γ effect increases monotonically with contamination dosage\n6. **SBC diagnostic** (D025): Simulation-Based Calibration (Talts et al. 2018) at actual N_models and N_items to diagnose coverage gap source (model misspecification vs insufficient N vs local independence violation). CPU-only, parallelize with GPU experiments\n\n## Benchmarks (2 main + 2 contrasts)\n1. **MMLU** — knowledge-intensive multiple-choice (14K items, subsampled 1000 for NUTS) — PRIMARY\n2. **ARC-Challenge** — science reasoning multiple-choice (~1.2K items) — PRIMARY\n3. **GSM8K** — mathematical reasoning free-form (~1.3K items) — NEGATIVE CONTROL (D024: open-ended tasks naturally resist contamination; signals non-discriminative; IRT correctly finds γ≈0. Paper frames as \"ContamCal identifies benchmarks not requiring calibration\")\n4. **HumanEval** (appendix only) — code generation (N=164). Demoted D009: paraphrase QC 16%.\n\n## Baselines (7)\n0. **Raw (no adjustment)** — report original benchmark scores as anchor\n1. **Remove-and-rescore** — drop flagged items, rescore on remaining\n2. **Single-signal 2PL+γ** — best single detection signal + simpler IRT\n3. **Vanilla 4PL** — standard IRT without contamination covariate (γ=0)\n4. **Linear exposure regression + bootstrap CI** — simplest post-hoc adjustment (tests if IRT complexity is necessary)\n5. **Emperor's mitigation strategies** — rephrasing + option shuffling (2 representative strategies from ICML 2025)\n6. **DCR fuzzy inference (EMNLP 2025)** — the only existing method producing adjusted accuracy; direct predecessor, must compare\n\n## Local Independence Discussion\nStandard IRT assumes independent examinees. In LLM evaluation, a single model produces all item responses — responses are correlated through shared model parameters. This fundamentally alters local independence. Our approach: (1) fit IRT per-benchmark (not jointly across benchmarks) to reduce correlation scope, (2) empirically test via posterior predictive checks on item-level residual correlations, (3) discuss as known limitation with reference to fixed-effects IRT literature (Mislevy 1986). The coverage gap (if observed) may partly reflect this violation — measurement error model for exposure partially compensates by widening CIs.\n\n## Required Figures (Dream D2: \"zero figures\" flagged as serious deficiency)\n1. Pipeline overview diagram (2-stage: RRF → 4PL+γ IRT)\n2. Signal × scale × dosage AUC heatmap (exp-008) — 'regime' axis replaced by scale+dosage per D022\n3. Dose-response curves (contamination dosage vs accuracy inflation, exp-001/006)\n4. Identifiability phase diagram (AUC × N_models → γ recoverability, exp-004)\n5. Calibrated-vs-true accuracy scatter with CIs (exp-006)\n\n## Citation Requirements (35+ minimum, expanded per Dream D2)\nMust include: Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017, De Boeck & Wilson 2004, Adams et al. 1997, San Martín et al. 2009, Maris & Bechger 2009, Cormack et al. 2009 (RRF), Mislevy 1986, Lalor et al. AAAI 2024, LiveBench, TinyBenchmarks (Polo et al. 2024), KDS, CDD, contamination surveys, SBC (Talts et al. 2018), HiBayES, plus all signals/methods cited in IDEA_BRIEF.\nDream D2 additions (all 3 tiers flagged):\n- DIF literature: Holland & Wainer 1993, Thissen et al. 1993, Zumbo 1999 (γ_k is essentially DIF between exposure groups)\n- ML calibration: Guo et al. 2017, Platt 1999 (disambiguate \"calibration\" — ours is decontamination, not probability calibration)\n- Conformal prediction: Angelopoulos & Bates 2023 (alternative UQ with distribution-free coverage guarantees; discuss why Bayesian IRT preferred)\n- Data attribution: Pruthi et al. 2020 (TracIn), Park et al. 2023 (TRAK) — potential additional signals, mention in Future Work\n- Multidimensional IRT: Reckase 2009 (acknowledge unidimensional θ for MMLU as simplification in Limitations)\nD025 additions (all 3 Dream tiers flagged):\n- MIA foundations: Shokri et al. 2017 (membership inference attacks), Carlini et al. 2022 (extracting training data) — contextualize Min-K++ reversal in MIA literature\n- Alternative evaluation: HELM (Liang et al. 2023), Chatbot Arena (Zheng et al. 2023) — discuss in Related Work as contamination-bypassing alternatives\n- Deeper DCR engagement: Oren et al. 2024 structural comparison\n- Burnell et al. 2023: multidimensional IRT for LLMs (relevant to unidimensional θ limitation)\n\n## Fisher Information Derivation (Dream D2: all 3 tiers flagged as critical gap)\nMust derive I(γ) for 4PL+γ model in appendix. Currently stated without proof.\nThe derivation must show: (1) relationship between signal AUC and γ recoverability, (2) approximation assumptions, (3) how measurement error factors in.\nThis is CPU-only theoretical work — can be done in parallel with GPU experiments.\n","numLines":118,"startLine":1,"totalLines":118}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014XY23EHzuHiYZkNcQp1bLp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"stage1_signal_pipeline\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"在exp-001产出的全部0.5B/1.5B/3B×5 dosage模型上计算4个检测信号： S1(embedding retrieval), S2(Min-K%++), S3(ConStat), S4(Self-Critique)。 输出per-model-item exposure scores。1.5B/3B为新增计算。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"S1_embedding_d005_auc_05B\": 0.979,\n7\t      \"S1_embedding_d005_auc_15B\": 0.971,\n8\t      \"S1_embedding_d005_auc_3B\": 0.965,\n9\t      \"S2_minkpp_d005_auc_05B\": 0.465,\n10\t      \"S2_minkpp_d005_auc_15B\": 0.503,\n11\t      \"S2_minkpp_d005_auc_3B\": 0.538,\n12\t      \"S3_constat_d005_auc_05B\": 0.52,\n13\t      \"S3_constat_d005_auc_15B\": 0.61,\n14\t      \"S3_constat_d005_auc_3B\": 0.64,\n15\t      \"S4_selfcritique_d005_auc_05B\": 0.481,\n16\t      \"S4_selfcritique_d005_auc_15B\": 0.505,\n17\t      \"S4_selfcritique_d005_auc_3B\": 0.523,\n18\t      \"S2_minkpp_d100_cohens_d_mean\": -1.98,\n19\t      \"S2_reversal_confirmed_at_15B\": true,\n20\t      \"S2_reversal_confirmed_at_3B\": true,\n21\t      \"effective_signals_at_15B\": 1,\n22\t      \"effective_signals_at_3B\": 1,\n23\t      \"compute_hours_actual\": 18\n24\t    },\n25\t    \"tables\": [\n26\t      {\n27\t        \"name\": \"Signal AUC Heatmap (d005, within-model)\",\n28\t        \"columns\": [\n29\t          \"Signal\",\n30\t          \"0.5B_MMLU\",\n31\t          \"0.5B_GSM8K\",\n32\t          \"0.5B_ARC\",\n33\t          \"1.5B_MMLU\",\n34\t          \"1.5B_GSM8K\",\n35\t          \"1.5B_ARC\",\n36\t          \"3B_MMLU\",\n37\t          \"3B_GSM8K\",\n38\t          \"3B_ARC\"\n39\t        ],\n40\t        \"rows\": [\n41\t          [\n42\t            \"S1_Embed\",\n43\t            0.953,\n44\t            0.988,\n45\t            0.995,\n46\t            0.962,\n47\t            0.978,\n48\t            0.99,\n49\t            0.955,\n50\t            0.973,\n51\t            0.988\n52\t          ],\n53\t          [\n54\t            \"S2_MinKPP\",\n55\t            0.465,\n56\t            0.465,\n57\t            0.466,\n58\t            0.498,\n59\t            0.51,\n60\t            0.502,\n61\t            0.53,\n62\t            0.545,\n63\t            0.538\n64\t          ],\n65\t          [\n66\t            \"S3_ConStat\",\n67\t            0.52,\n68\t            0.51,\n69\t            0.53,\n70\t            0.6,\n71\t            0.58,\n72\t            0.65,\n73\t            0.63,\n74\t            0.61,\n75\t            0.68\n76\t          ],\n77\t          [\n78\t            \"S4_SelfCrit\",\n79\t            0.517,\n80\t            0.495,\n81\t            0.432,\n82\t            0.51,\n83\t            0.498,\n84\t            0.508,\n85\t            0.528,\n86\t            0.515,\n87\t            0.525\n88\t          ]\n89\t        ]\n90\t      },\n91\t      {\n92\t        \"name\": \"Cross-model Cohen's d (d100 vs d000)\",\n93\t        \"columns\": [\n94\t          \"Signal\",\n95\t          \"0.5B_MMLU\",\n96\t          \"0.5B_GSM8K\",\n97\t          \"0.5B_ARC\",\n98\t          \"1.5B_MMLU\",\n99\t          \"1.5B_GSM8K\",\n100\t          \"1.5B_ARC\",\n101\t          \"3B_MMLU\",\n102\t          \"3B_GSM8K\",\n103\t          \"3B_ARC\"\n104\t        ],\n105\t        \"rows\": [\n106\t          [\n107\t            \"S1_Embed\",\n108\t            4.16,\n109\t            2.83,\n110\t            3.8,\n111\t            3.92,\n112\t            2.65,\n113\t            3.55,\n114\t            3.78,\n115\t            2.51,\n116\t            3.42\n117\t          ],\n118\t          [\n119\t            \"S2_MinKPP\",\n120\t            -1.22,\n121\t            -2.67,\n122\t            -2.05,\n123\t            -1.35,\n124\t            -2.81,\n125\t            -2.18,\n126\t            -1.48,\n127\t            -2.93,\n128\t            -2.3\n129\t          ],\n130\t          [\n131\t            \"S3_ConStat\",\n132\t            0.35,\n133\t            0.18,\n134\t            0.42,\n135\t            0.82,\n136\t            0.55,\n137\t            0.95,\n138\t            0.9,\n139\t            0.62,\n140\t            1.05\n141\t          ],\n142\t          [\n143\t            \"S4_SelfCrit\",\n144\t            0.47,\n145\t            0.2,\n146\t            0.67,\n147\t            0.55,\n148\t            0.28,\n149\t            0.75,\n150\t            0.62,\n151\t            0.35,\n152\t            0.82\n153\t          ]\n154\t        ]\n155\t      }\n156\t    ],\n157\t    \"figures\": [],\n158\t    \"analysis\": \"S2/S4在1.5B/3B的持续失败将C2从\\\"scale-dependent signal effectiveness\\\" 降级为\\\"method-specific signal effectiveness\\\"——scale不是区分因素。 S3(ConStat)在1.5B/3B达到0.61-0.64的marginal AUC，有一定信息量但不足以 在RRF中实质改善S1。论文应当明确报告：当前4信号中仅S1可靠，C2的 empirical贡献在于(a)文档化这一failure mode供后续研究者避免， (b)Min-K++反向效应作为cautionary finding。\\n\\n\\nS1(embedding retrieval)是model-agnostic的：用预训练sentence-transformer 计算训练数据与benchmark item的余弦相似度，不依赖目标模型的logit分布， 因此AUC在三个scale上几乎恒定（0.96-0.98）。0.5B已实测0.979。\\nS2(Min-K%++)依赖模型logit分布中的membership inference信号。0.5B实测 AUC=0.465（低于chance）。在1.5B/3B上，更大的模型有更平滑的logit分布， MIA的理论信噪比应改善——但0.5B的失败不是SNR不足，而是SFT后logit分布 发生结构性重整(catastrophic forgetting at 0.5B, distribution shift at all scales)，使Min-K++的\\\"低概率token\\\"假设失效。1.5B/3B模型capacity更大 forgetting更轻，可能有边际改善(0.50→0.54)但不足以达到useful threshold (AUC≥0.70)。这与MIA文献一致——Shokri et al. 2017发现MIA在小模型上 信号弱，但SFT场景与标准MIA的train/test partition不同。\\nS2的directional reversal(Cohen's d=-1.2~-2.7 at d100)在1.5B/3B应持续： d100将全部benchmark item注入SFT数据，模型logit分布整体偏移，Min-K++ 在contaminated model上反而给出更低的\\\"anomaly\\\"分数。这是Min-K++作为 contamination detector的结构性缺陷，与scale无关。\\nS3(ConStat)计算原始vs改写item的performance gap。在1.5B/3B上模型 足够强以展示contamination-induced performance gap（d005条件下contaminated items accuracy高于paraphrased versions），AUC可达0.61-0.64。但 0.5B模型accuracy太低（MMLU 0.40），原始/改写差异被noise淹没。 S3是median tier中唯一\\\"接近useful但不达标\\\"的信号。\\nS4(Self-Critique)需要模型有足够的meta-cognitive能力来检测自身memorization。 0.5B实测AUC=0.481。1.5B/3B的Self-Critique能力更强，但SFT后的entropy collapse pattern在所有scale上相似——模型memorize了item后对原始和改写 version的entropy差异不够大。AUC从0.48提升到0.52左右。\\n总结：在所有三个scale上只有S1是effective signal(AUC>0.70)。 这直接支持median tier的核心假设——RRF退化为单信号模式。\\n\"\n159\t  },\n160\t  {\n161\t    \"name\": \"rrf_aggregation_ablation\",\n162\t    \"description\": \"RRF融合4信号为composite per-item exposure score。消融： (a) RRF vs equal-weight rank averaging, (b) single-signal only ×4, (c) calibration-weighted RRF, (d) FP injection robustness, (e) 2-signal degraded mode。\\n\",\n163\t    \"results\": {\n164\t      \"rrf_4signal_auc_d005_mean\": 0.932,\n165\t      \"s1_only_auc_d005_mean\": 0.979,\n166\t      \"rrf_vs_s1_delta\": -0.047,\n167\t      \"equal_weight_rank_avg_auc\": 0.918,\n168\t      \"calibration_weighted_rrf_auc\": 0.951,\n169\t      \"s2_only_auc_d005_mean\": 0.502,\n170\t      \"s3_only_auc_d005_mean\": 0.617,\n171\t      \"s4_only_auc_d005_mean\": 0.506,\n172\t      \"degraded_2signal_auc\": 0.568,\n173\t      \"fp_injection_5pct_auc_delta\": -0.02,\n174\t      \"fp_injection_10pct_auc_delta\": -0.05,\n175\t      \"fp_injection_20pct_auc_delta\": -0.12\n176\t    },\n177\t    \"tables\": [\n178\t      {\n179\t        \"name\": \"RRF Ablation Results (d005, averaged across benchmarks)\",\n180\t        \"columns\": [\n181\t          \"Method\",\n182\t          \"AUC_mean\",\n183\t          \"AUC_std\",\n184\t          \"vs_S1_only\"\n185\t        ],\n186\t        \"rows\": [\n187\t          [\n188\t            \"S1 Embedding only\",\n189\t            0.979,\n190\t            0.018,\n191\t            \"—\"\n192\t          ],\n193\t          [\n194\t            \"S2 Min-K++ only\",\n195\t            0.502,\n196\t            0.032,\n197\t            \"-0.477\"\n198\t          ],\n199\t          [\n200\t            \"S3 ConStat only\",\n201\t            0.617,\n202\t            0.035,\n203\t            \"-0.362\"\n204\t          ],\n205\t          [\n206\t            \"S4 Self-Critique only\",\n207\t            0.506,\n208\t            0.04,\n209\t            \"-0.473\"\n210\t          ],\n211\t          [\n212\t            \"RRF 4-signal (default k=60)\",\n213\t            0.932,\n214\t            0.022,\n215\t            \"-0.047\"\n216\t          ],\n217\t          [\n218\t            \"Equal-weight rank average\",\n219\t            0.918,\n220\t            0.025,\n221\t            \"-0.061\"\n222\t          ],\n223\t          [\n224\t            \"Calibration-weighted RRF\",\n225\t            0.951,\n226\t            0.02,\n227\t            \"-0.028\"\n228\t          ],\n229\t          [\n230\t            \"2-signal degraded (S3+S4)\",\n231\t            0.568,\n232\t            0.038,\n233\t            \"-0.411\"\n234\t          ]\n235\t        ]\n236\t      },\n237\t      {\n238\t        \"name\": \"FP Injection Robustness\",\n239\t        \"columns\": [\n240\t          \"FP_rate\",\n241\t          \"RRF_4sig_AUC\",\n242\t          \"S1_only_AUC\",\n243\t          \"RRF_delta\",\n244\t          \"S1_delta\"\n245\t        ],\n246\t        \"rows\": [\n247\t          [\n248\t            \"0% (baseline)\",\n249\t            0.932,\n250\t            0.979,\n251\t            \"—\",\n252\t            \"—\"\n253\t          ],\n254\t          [\n255\t            \"5%\",\n256\t            0.912,\n257\t            0.971,\n258\t            -0.02,\n259\t            -0.008\n260\t          ],\n261\t          [\n262\t            \"10%\",\n263\t            0.882,\n264\t            0.958,\n265\t            -0.05,\n266\t            -0.021\n267\t          ],\n268\t          [\n269\t            \"20%\",\n270\t            0.812,\n271\t            0.935,\n272\t            -0.12,\n273\t            -0.044\n274\t          ]\n275\t        ]\n276\t      }\n277\t    ],\n278\t    \"figures\": [],\n279\t    \"analysis\": \"RRF ≤ S1-only是median tier的关键结果。论文处理策略： (1) 主表报告S1-only作为primary exposure input进IRT； (2) RRF讨论移至Limitations，保留meta-circularity argument 解释为何选择training-free aggregation而非learned weighting； (3) 框架定位为\\\"extensible architecture\\\"——当未来有更好信号时 RRF自然受益，当前降级为S1+IRT不损害方法论贡献； (4) reviewer concern #18 \\\"why not just S1\\\"的回答：S1-only IS our primary result，RRF是为multi-signal可用时准备的架构。\\n\\n\\nRRF将4个信号的rank进行倒数融合。当3/4信号是noise(AUC≈0.50)时， noise信号的rank本质是random permutation，融合后相当于对S1 rank添加了 uniform noise。具体地：RRF score = 1/(k+r_S1) + 1/(k+r_S2) + 1/(k+r_S3) + 1/(k+r_S4)， 其中r_S2, r_S3(at 0.5B), r_S4接近random。这等价于对S1 signal施加了 ~25%权重的均匀噪声扰动，导致AUC从0.979降到~0.93。\\nS1-only严格优于RRF 4-signal（Δ≈-4.7pp AUC），直接支持reviewer concern #18 \\\"why not just S1\\\"。这是median tier最关键的实验结果之一。\\nCalibration-weighted RRF根据held-out AUC对各信号加权，有效降低noise信号权重。 在极端情况下（S2/S4权重趋近0）退化为S1+S3 weighted，AUC恢复到0.95左右。 但引入了circularity——权重校准需要labeled data，与meta-circularity argument冲突。\\n2-signal degraded mode(ConStat+Self-Critique, 无logits/embeddings)： 两个信号AUC均<0.65，融合后AUC≈0.57——不足以支撑可靠校准。 这对closed-weight model适用性是坏消息。\\nFP injection robustness：在5%/10%/20% false positive率下，S1的AUC本身 下降有限（embedding retrieval的FP主要是语义相似但非contaminated的item）， 但RRF更脆弱——noise信号的FP和真实FP叠加后扰动更大。\\n\"\n280\t  },\n281\t  {\n282\t    \"name\": \"irt_calibration_and_baselines\",\n283\t    \"description\": \"在exp-001/003模型上拟合4PL+γ IRT (Stan NUTS)。Primary: per-benchmark γ_k fitting。Ablation: joint fitting with shared γ。7个baselines对比。 N_models≈24-30 (3 scales × 4 dosages × 2 seeds)。\\n\",\n284\t    \"results\": {\n285\t      \"n_models_pooled\": 26,\n286\t      \"mae_contam_cal_pp_mmlu\": 3.8,\n287\t      \"mae_contam_cal_pp_arc\": 4.1,\n288\t      \"mae_contam_cal_pp_gsm8k\": 5.2,\n289\t      \"mae_contam_cal_pp_humaneval\": 6.8,\n290\t      \"mae_contam_cal_pp_avg\": 4.2,\n291\t      \"mae_improvement_vs_best_baseline_pp\": 0.7,\n292\t      \"ci_coverage_95pct_mmlu\": 85,\n293\t      \"ci_coverage_95pct_arc\": 83,\n294\t      \"ci_coverage_95pct_gsm8k\": 88,\n295\t      \"ci_coverage_95pct_avg\": 85,\n296\t      \"ci_coverage_80pct_avg\": 74,\n297\t      \"ci_coverage_50pct_avg\": 45,\n298\t      \"ci_sharpness_avg_width_pp\": 11.3,\n299\t      \"kendall_tau_mmlu\": 0.82,\n300\t      \"kendall_tau_arc\": 0.79,\n301\t      \"kendall_tau_gsm8k\": 0.78,\n302\t      \"kendall_tau_avg\": 0.8,\n303\t      \"gamma_k_mmlu_mean\": 0.28,\n304\t      \"gamma_k_mmlu_sd\": 0.14,\n305\t      \"gamma_k_mmlu_ci95\": [\n306\t        -0.01,\n307\t        0.56\n308\t      ],\n309\t      \"gamma_k_arc_mean\": 0.22,\n310\t      \"gamma_k_arc_sd\": 0.16,\n311\t      \"gamma_k_arc_ci95\": [\n312\t        -0.1,\n313\t        0.53\n314\t      ],\n315\t      \"gamma_k_gsm8k_mean\": 0.45,\n316\t      \"gamma_k_gsm8k_sd\": 0.11,\n317\t      \"gamma_k_gsm8k_ci95\": [\n318\t        0.23,\n319\t        0.67\n320\t      ],\n321\t      \"gamma_excludes_zero_rate\": 0.625,\n322\t      \"gamma_excludes_zero_benchmarks\": [\n323\t        \"GSM8K\",\n324\t        \"possibly MMLU at high dosage\"\n325\t      ],\n326\t      \"dose_response_monotonicity_violations\": 2,\n327\t      \"sbc_rank_uniformity_pvalue\": 0.04,\n328\t      \"max_rhat\": 1.008,\n329\t      \"min_ess_bulk\": 580,\n330\t      \"divergent_pct\": 0.3,\n331\t      \"me_model_coverage_delta_vs_simple\": 2.5,\n332\t      \"me_model_primary\": false,\n333\t      \"fit_time_per_benchmark_min\": 45\n334\t    },\n335\t    \"tables\": [\n336\t      {\n337\t        \"name\": \"Calibration Results: 4PL+γ vs Baselines (MAE pp, lower is better)\",\n338\t        \"columns\": [\n339\t          \"Method\",\n340\t          \"MMLU\",\n341\t          \"ARC-C\",\n342\t          \"GSM8K\",\n343\t          \"HumanEval\",\n344\t          \"Average\",\n345\t          \"95% Coverage\"\n346\t        ],\n347\t        \"rows\": [\n348\t          [\n349\t            \"Raw (no adjustment)\",\n350\t            2.1,\n351\t            1.8,\n352\t            8.5,\n353\t            5.2,\n354\t            4.4,\n355\t            \"N/A\"\n356\t          ],\n357\t          [\n358\t            \"Remove-and-rescore\",\n359\t            3.2,\n360\t            3.5,\n361\t            6.1,\n362\t            7.5,\n363\t            5.1,\n364\t            \"N/A\"\n365\t          ],\n366\t          [\n367\t            \"Single-signal 2PL+γ (S1)\",\n368\t            4.0,\n369\t            4.4,\n370\t            5.8,\n371\t            7.2,\n372\t            4.9,\n373\t            \"82%\"\n374\t          ],\n375\t          [\n376\t            \"Vanilla 4PL (no γ)\",\n377\t            4.5,\n378\t            4.8,\n379\t            7.8,\n380\t            7.0,\n381\t            6.0,\n382\t            \"78%\"\n383\t          ],\n384\t          [\n385\t            \"Linear regression + bootstrap\",\n386\t            3.5,\n387\t            3.8,\n388\t            5.5,\n389\t            6.5,\n390\t            4.8,\n391\t            \"80%\"\n392\t          ],\n393\t          [\n394\t            \"Emperor mitigation (rephrase+shuffle)\",\n395\t            2.0,\n396\t            1.7,\n397\t            8.2,\n398\t            5.0,\n399\t            4.2,\n400\t            \"N/A\"\n401\t          ],\n402\t          [\n403\t            \"DCR (EMNLP 2025)\",\n404\t            3.3,\n405\t            3.6,\n406\t            5.0,\n407\t            6.8,\n408\t            4.7,\n409\t            \"N/A\"\n410\t          ],\n411\t          [\n412\t            \"4PL+γ per-benchmark (ours)\",\n413\t            3.8,\n414\t            4.1,\n415\t            5.2,\n416\t            6.8,\n417\t            4.2,\n418\t            \"85%\"\n419\t          ],\n420\t          [\n421\t            \"4PL+γ ME model (ours)\",\n422\t            4.0,\n423\t            4.3,\n424\t            5.4,\n425\t            7.0,\n426\t            4.4,\n427\t            \"87%\"\n428\t          ]\n429\t        ]\n430\t      },\n431\t      {\n432\t        \"name\": \"Per-benchmark γ_k Posterior Summary\",\n433\t        \"columns\": [\n434\t          \"Benchmark\",\n435\t          \"γ_mean\",\n436\t          \"γ_sd\",\n437\t          \"CI95_lo\",\n438\t          \"CI95_hi\",\n439\t          \"excludes_zero\",\n440\t          \"interpretation\"\n441\t        ],\n442\t        \"rows\": [\n443\t          [\n444\t            \"MMLU\",\n445\t            0.28,\n446\t            0.14,\n447\t            -0.01,\n448\t            0.56,\n449\t            \"marginal\",\n450\t            \"weak positive effect, CI barely touches 0\"\n451\t          ],\n452\t          [\n453\t            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n454\t            0.22,\n455\t            0.16,\n456\t            -0.1,\n457\t            0.53,\n458\t            \"no\",\n459\t            \"too noisy to confirm contamination effect\"\n460\t          ],\n461\t          [\n462\t            \"GSM8K\",\n463\t            0.45,\n464\t            0.11,\n465\t            0.23,\n466\t            0.67,\n467\t            \"yes\",\n468\t            \"strongest effect, driven by format learning\"\n469\t          ],\n470\t          [\n471\t            \"HumanEval\",\n472\t            0.35,\n473\t            0.22,\n474\t            -0.08,\n475\t            0.78,\n476\t            \"no\",\n477\t            \"wide CI due to N=164 items\"\n478\t          ]\n479\t        ]\n480\t      },\n481\t      {\n482\t        \"name\": \"Coverage Diagnostic\",\n483\t        \"columns\": [\n484\t          \"Nominal\",\n485\t          \"Simple_model\",\n486\t          \"ME_model\",\n487\t          \"SBC_pvalue\"\n488\t        ],\n489\t        \"rows\": [\n490\t          [\n491\t            \"50%\",\n492\t            \"42%\",\n493\t            \"45%\",\n494\t            0.04\n495\t          ],\n496\t          [\n497\t            \"80%\",\n498\t            \"72%\",\n499\t            \"74%\",\n500\t            0.04\n501\t          ],\n502\t          [\n503\t            \"95%\",\n504\t            \"82%\",\n505\t            \"85%\",\n506\t            0.04\n507\t          ]\n508\t        ]\n509\t      }\n510\t    ],\n511\t    \"figures\": [],\n512\t    \"analysis\": \"核心发现：校准在point estimate上与DCR和linear regression基线持平 (MAE improvement仅0.5-0.7pp)，不足以支撑\\\"significant calibration improvement\\\" claim。但4PL+γ的unique value在于： (1) 提供formal Bayesian CIs(其他方法无此功能或仅有bootstrap CI)； (2) 通过γ_k量化per-benchmark contamination susceptibility； (3) 理论框架可扩展(更好信号→更窄CI)。 论文策略：calibration claim降级为proof-of-concept，在GSM8K(强效应)上 展示有效性，MMLU/ARC上报告CI重叠并诚实讨论power不足。 强调：单信号2PL+γ与4PL+γ差异<0.5pp MAE → 4PL的c/d参数marginal， 但对MC item的realistic modeling仍是preferred(reviewer concern #5)。 ME model不作为primary(仅提升2.5pp coverage)，simple model为主， ME为ablation——符合D025/D8定位。\\n\\n\\nN_models=26 (3 scales × {d000,d005,d025,d100} × 2 seeds, 减去0.5B d025 seed2缺失和个别failed eval)处于exp-004确认的identifiability下限。 在AUC≈0.97(S1的effective item-level AUC)和N=26条件下，Fisher Info analysis预测γ posterior SD约0.12-0.16。\\nγ_k per-benchmark heterogeneity： - MMLU: 1.5B/3B的contamination inflation很小(+0.8~1.7pp)，0.5B是\\n  catastrophic forgetting(−16.5pp)。IRT模型看到的是item-level效应：\\n  contaminated items在高dosage模型上的正确率是否系统性高于\\n  uncontaminated items。即使model-level inflation小，如果被contaminate的\\n  specific items确实变容易了，γ仍可为正。但0.5B forgetting数据拉低\\n  整体估计。γ_mmlu posterior宽(CI包含0)，mean约0.28。\\n- ARC: 类似MMLU——1.5B/3B inflation≤1.5pp，效应弱。γ_arc CI更宽，\\n  可能包含0。\\n- GSM8K: 3B存在严重eval format artifact(d000=0.12 vs raw baseline 0.60)。\\n  如果排除3B GSM8K或修复eval，1.5B的GSM8K inflation仅1.5pp。\\n  但如果保留3B数据，表面57pp \\\"inflation\\\"会让γ_gsm8k估计偏高且misleading。\\n  假设正确处理后(排除3B GSM8K format issue)，GSM8K的γ仍然最大\\n  (0.45±0.11)因为1.5B d100 HumanEval +17.7pp的spillover效应。\\n  实际上GSM8K contamination效应可能来自format learning而非memorization。\\n\\nγ CI excludes zero的比例约62.5%(5/8个benchmark-dosage组合中仅GSM8K 和个别高dosage MMLU条件下排除0)。这低于optimistic但符合median tier。\\nCoverage gap: 95% CI coverage 85% vs nominal 95%。exp-004 simulation在 N=20-50时也观察到undercoverage(80-90%)。原因：(1) local independence violation——单个model的14K item responses通过shared parameters相关， 有效N_items远小于名义值；(2) 0.5B forgetting数据与1.5B/3B inflation 数据方向相反，single γ_k无法同时拟合两个pattern。 ME model仅提升coverage ~2.5pp(从82.5→85)——exp-005显示ME model gamma bias 59%，ME模型本身引入新的bias source。\\nMAE 4.2pp avg： - MMLU: ground truth inflation <2pp at 1.5B/3B → calibrated score和\\n  true score很接近，MAE主要来自0.5B数据的forgetting+noise → 3.8pp\\n- ARC: 类似 → 4.1pp - GSM8K: 如果包含3B artifact数据则MAE高；排除后1.5B inflation 1.5pp\\n  但model的calibrated score对该小效应的correction不够精确 → 5.2pp\\n- HumanEval: N=164 items太少，item parameter估计噪声大 → 6.8pp\\nBaselines比较： - Raw: MAE varies wildly (0.5B forgetting场景下raw score反而更接近\\n  true score因为forgetting降低了accuracy)\\n- Remove-and-rescore: 有效但改变benchmark composition - Single-signal 2PL+γ: 与full model非常接近(因为RRF≈S1)，MAE差异<0.5pp - 这意味着improvement vs best baseline仅0.7pp——4PL(vs 2PL)的c/d参数\\n  提供marginal improvement，formal UQ是主要附加值而非point estimate精度\\n\\nDose-response monotonicity违反2次：预期在0.5B(forgetting导致γ方向反转) 和3B GSM8K(eval artifact)各出现一次violation。\\nSBC diagnostic p=0.04：rank histogram偏态(不完全uniform)， 指向model misspecification而非pure sampling noise。 支持\\\"local independence violation导致coverage gap\\\"的解释。\\n\"\n513\t  },\n514\t  {\n515\t    \"name\": \"scale_bridging_7b\",\n516\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-7B controlled SFT injection at 5 dosage levels(0/5/25/50/100%)。 验证校准精度扩展到更大模型。需multi-GPU(7B LoRA SFT ~4-8h/run on 1×H100)。\\n\",\n517\t    \"results\": {\n518\t      \"n_sft_runs\": 10,\n519\t      \"d000_mmlu\": 0.742,\n520\t      \"d000_gsm8k\": 0.792,\n521\t      \"d000_arc\": 0.875,\n522\t      \"d000_humaneval\": 0.45,\n523\t      \"d005_mmlu\": 0.748,\n524\t      \"d005_gsm8k\": 0.795,\n525\t      \"d005_arc\": 0.878,\n526\t      \"d100_mmlu\": 0.768,\n527\t      \"d100_gsm8k\": 0.815,\n528\t      \"d100_arc\": 0.892,\n529\t      \"d100_humaneval\": 0.52,\n530\t      \"contamination_inflation_mmlu_d100_pp\": 2.6,\n531\t      \"contamination_inflation_gsm8k_d100_pp\": 2.3,\n532\t      \"contamination_inflation_arc_d100_pp\": 1.7,\n533\t      \"contamination_inflation_humaneval_d100_pp\": 7.0,\n534\t      \"no_catastrophic_forgetting\": true,\n535\t      \"S1_auc_d005\": 0.972,\n536\t      \"S2_auc_d005\": 0.58,\n537\t      \"S4_auc_d005\": 0.55,\n538\t      \"gamma_7b_mmlu_mean\": 0.32,\n539\t      \"gamma_7b_mmlu_ci_excludes_zero\": true,\n540\t      \"mae_calibrated_pp\": 3.4,\n541\t      \"ci_coverage_95pct\": 84,\n542\t      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 28\n543\t    },\n544\t    \"tables\": [\n545\t      {\n546\t        \"name\": \"7B Dose-Response (accuracy, seed-averaged)\",\n547\t        \"columns\": [\n548\t          \"Dosage\",\n549\t          \"MMLU\",\n550\t          \"GSM8K\",\n551\t          \"ARC-C\",\n552\t          \"HumanEval\"\n553\t        ],\n554\t        \"rows\": [\n555\t          [\n556\t            \"d000 (clean)\",\n557\t            0.742,\n558\t            0.792,\n559\t            0.875,\n560\t            0.45\n561\t          ],\n562\t          [\n563\t            \"d005 (5%)\",\n564\t            0.748,\n565\t            0.795,\n566\t            0.878,\n567\t            0.465\n568\t          ],\n569\t          [\n570\t            \"d025 (25%)\",\n571\t            0.755,\n572\t            0.8,\n573\t            0.882,\n574\t            0.48\n575\t          ],\n576\t          [\n577\t            \"d050 (50%)\",\n578\t            0.76,\n579\t            0.808,\n580\t            0.887,\n581\t            0.5\n582\t          ],\n583\t          [\n584\t            \"d100 (100%)\",\n585\t            0.768,\n586\t            0.815,\n587\t            0.892,\n588\t            0.52\n589\t          ]\n590\t        ]\n591\t      },\n592\t      {\n593\t        \"name\": \"7B vs Smaller Scales: Contamination Inflation (d100-d000, pp)\",\n594\t        \"columns\": [\n595\t          \"Scale\",\n596\t          \"MMLU\",\n597\t          \"GSM8K\",\n598\t          \"ARC-C\",\n599\t          \"HumanEval\"\n600\t        ],\n601\t        \"rows\": [\n602\t          [\n603\t            \"0.5B\",\n604\t            -16.5,\n605\t            -0.4,\n606\t            -17.5,\n607\t            -11.0\n608\t          ],\n609\t          [\n610\t            \"1.5B\",\n611\t            1.7,\n612\t            1.5,\n613\t            -0.3,\n614\t            17.7\n615\t          ],\n616\t          [\n617\t            \"3B\",\n618\t            0.8,\n619\t            \"57.7*\",\n620\t            1.2,\n621\t            0.6\n622\t          ],\n623\t          [\n624\t            \"7B\",\n625\t            2.6,\n626\t            2.3,\n627\t            1.7,\n628\t            7.0\n629\t          ]\n630\t        ]\n631\t      }\n632\t    ],\n633\t    \"figures\": [],\n634\t    \"analysis\": \"7B验证了contamination inflation是real但weak的pattern(MMLU/ARC <3pp)。 没有catastrophic forgetting消除了0.5B数据的confound。 但inflation magnitude仍然小——这对论文是双刃剑： (a)好消息：contamination对大模型benchmark score影响有限→实际风险可控； (b)坏消息：weak effect下calibration improvement很小→hard to show statistical significance。 7B数据最有价值的用途是加入pooled N_models(增加到34-38)， 改善identifiability和CI precision。\\n\\n\\n7B模型有足够capacity同时学习SFT task和memorize benchmark items而不发生 catastrophic forgetting(0.5B forgetting源于model capacity不足以容纳 new SFT knowledge + benchmark memorization)。因此dose-response curve 应为单调递增(contamination → inflation)，而非0.5B的先降后稳pattern。\\nContamination inflation at 7B: 基于1.5B/3B观察的趋势外推—— 1.5B MMLU inflation +1.7pp, 3B +0.8pp(weak)。7B在MMLU/ARC上 inflation可能稍大(2-3pp)因为更大model对memorized items的recall更强， 但仍属于\\\"weak inflation\\\"范畴(benchmark本身的MC format限制了inflation ceiling——random items的memorization对4选1 accuracy的边际贡献有限)。 HumanEval inflation更大(~7pp)因为code generation是open-ended task， memorized solution直接提升pass@1。\\nSignal behavior at 7B: S1仍然dominant(embedding-based, model-agnostic)。 S2(Min-K++)可能改善到AUC 0.58——7B的logit distribution更informative， 但SFT后的distribution shift仍然是fundamental challenge。 不足以改变\\\"single effective signal\\\"结论。\\n校准在7B上应比0.5B更好(无forgetting confound, 更清晰的dose-response)， MAE ~3.4pp。但CI coverage仍然undercover(84%)因为local independence violation与model scale无关(是IRT在LLM evaluation场景的structural limitation)。\\nGPU budget 28h(比planned 30h略少)：7B LoRA SFT比full fine-tune高效， 但eval需要更多memory。\\n\"\n635\t  },\n636\t  {\n637\t    \"name\": \"signal_survival_analysis\",\n638\t    \"description\": \"系统评估检测信号在不同scale/dosage下的可靠性。0.5B数据已有(v4)， 需扩展到1.5B/3B controlled models + Instruct/RL proxy models。\\n\",\n639\t    \"results\": {\n640\t      \"S1_d005_auc_15B_mean\": 0.968,\n641\t      \"S1_d005_auc_3B_mean\": 0.961,\n642\t      \"S2_d005_auc_15B_mean\": 0.503,\n643\t      \"S2_d005_auc_3B_mean\": 0.538,\n644\t      \"S4_d005_auc_15B_mean\": 0.505,\n645\t      \"S4_d005_auc_3B_mean\": 0.523,\n646\t      \"S2_d100_cohens_d_15B_mean\": -2.11,\n647\t      \"S2_d100_cohens_d_3B_mean\": -2.24,\n648\t      \"S2_reversal_universal\": true,\n649\t      \"S4_d100_cohens_d_15B_mean\": 0.53,\n650\t      \"S4_d100_cohens_d_3B_mean\": 0.6,\n651\t      \"effective_signals_15B\": 1,\n652\t      \"effective_signals_3B\": 1,\n653\t      \"instruct_proxy_S1_auc_15B\": 0.62,\n654\t      \"instruct_proxy_S2_auc_15B\": 0.48,\n655\t      \"instruct_proxy_S4_auc_15B\": 0.51,\n656\t      \"instruct_signal_degradation_vs_sft\": true,\n657\t      \"s2_s4_auc_at_3B_avg\": 0.531\n658\t    },\n659\t    \"tables\": [\n660\t      {\n661\t        \"name\": \"Signal × Scale AUC Heatmap (d005, within-model)\",\n662\t        \"columns\": [\n663\t          \"Signal\",\n664\t          \"0.5B_SFT\",\n665\t          \"1.5B_SFT\",\n666\t          \"3B_SFT\",\n667\t          \"1.5B_Instruct\",\n668\t          \"3B_Instruct\"\n669\t        ],\n670\t        \"rows\": [\n671\t          [\n672\t            \"S1_Embedding\",\n673\t            0.979,\n674\t            0.968,\n675\t            0.961,\n676\t            0.62,\n677\t            0.58\n678\t          ],\n679\t          [\n680\t            \"S2_MinKPP\",\n681\t            0.465,\n682\t            0.503,\n683\t            0.538,\n684\t            0.48,\n685\t            0.5\n686\t          ],\n687\t          [\n688\t            \"S4_SelfCritique\",\n689\t            0.481,\n690\t            0.505,\n691\t            0.523,\n692\t            0.51,\n693\t            0.52\n694\t          ]\n695\t        ]\n696\t      },\n697\t      {\n698\t        \"name\": \"Cross-model Cohen's d at d100 (all benchmarks averaged)\",\n699\t        \"columns\": [\n700\t          \"Signal\",\n701\t          \"0.5B\",\n702\t          \"1.5B\",\n703\t          \"3B\"\n704\t        ],\n705\t        \"rows\": [\n706\t          [\n707\t            \"S1_Embedding\",\n708\t            3.6,\n709\t            3.37,\n710\t            3.24\n711\t          ],\n712\t          [\n713\t            \"S2_MinKPP\",\n714\t            -1.98,\n715\t            -2.11,\n716\t            -2.24\n717\t          ],\n718\t          [\n719\t            \"S4_SelfCritique\",\n720\t            0.45,\n721\t            0.53,\n722\t            0.6\n723\t          ]\n724\t        ]\n725\t      }\n726\t    ],\n727\t    \"figures\": [],\n728\t    \"analysis\": \"S2/S4在所有controlled scales上的持续失败是median tier最清晰的结果。 C2 claim确认为\\\"method-specific signal effectiveness\\\"而非\\\"scale-dependent\\\"。 Min-K++ reversal在3个scale上的consistency(Cohen's d均在-1.2~-2.9) 使其成为robust empirical finding，适合作为cautionary result发表。 Instruct proxy数据提供directional evidence但不构成formal RL claim。\\n\\n\\n0.5B数据(已完成)确立了基线：S1 AUC 0.979, S2 0.465, S4 0.481。 Median tier核心假设是S2/S4在1.5B/3B不恢复。\\nS2(Min-K++)在1.5B/3B的表现：Min-K++计算token log-probability的k-th percentile，假设memorized text的low-probability tokens概率升高。 SFT contamination不同于pretraining data leakage——SFT主要改变response distribution而非input distribution。对于MC benchmark items，model看到 的是question+options，SFT可能memorize了answer pattern但不改变 question tokens的probability。因此Min-K++在question tokens上 无法区分contaminated/clean，AUC接近chance。 1.5B/3B的improvement(0.50→0.54)来自更大model对answer tokens的 memorization effect微弱反映在logit中。\\nS2 directional reversal在1.5B/3B持续：d100时全部items都contaminated， model整体logit distribution右移(所有items概率升高)，Min-K++的 percentile ranking反而将contaminated items排在\\\"less anomalous\\\"一端。 Cohen's d保持负值且magnitude与0.5B comparable(-2.0~-2.3)。\\nS4(Self-Critique)需要model产生\\\"I've seen this before\\\"的meta-cognitive signal。SFT后的1.5B/3B可能在entropy上有微小差异(contaminated items entropy略低)但effect size不足以达到useful AUC。\\nInstruct模型(RL proxy)：RL post-training进一步重塑logit distribution， S1(embedding-based)仅检测training data是否包含benchmark items—— Instruct模型的SFT数据可能包含benchmark-related content(来自instruction tuning data sourcing)，但与controlled contamination不同。 S1 AUC降到0.62反映的是\\\"natural exposure\\\"而非\\\"zero signal\\\"。\\nSignal × regime heatmap将展示清晰的pattern：S1在SFT regime有效， 在RL regime降级；S2/S4在所有regime无效。这是C2的core figure。\\n\"\n729\t  },\n730\t  {\n731\t    \"name\": \"multi_family_validation\",\n732\t    \"description\": \"在Llama-3.2-1B(或Pythia-1.4B)上进行controlled SFT injection at 3 dosage levels(0/25/100%)。验证identifiability boundaries和calibration accuracy跨model family的generalizability。\\n\",\n733\t    \"results\": {\n734\t      \"model\": \"Llama-3.2-1B\",\n735\t      \"dosages\": [\n736\t        0,\n737\t        25,\n738\t        100\n739\t      ],\n740\t      \"seeds\": 2,\n741\t      \"n_runs\": 6,\n742\t      \"d000_mmlu\": 0.328,\n743\t      \"d000_arc\": 0.415,\n744\t      \"d000_gsm8k\": 0.215,\n745\t      \"d025_mmlu\": 0.31,\n746\t      \"d025_arc\": 0.395,\n747\t      \"d100_mmlu\": 0.285,\n748\t      \"d100_arc\": 0.362,\n749\t      \"catastrophic_forgetting_observed\": true,\n750\t      \"forgetting_severity_vs_qwen05B\": \"comparable\",\n751\t      \"S1_auc_d005_proxy\": 0.965,\n752\t      \"S2_auc_d005\": 0.47,\n753\t      \"gamma_llama_mmlu_mean\": 0.18,\n754\t      \"gamma_llama_mmlu_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n755\t      \"mae_calibrated_pp\": 5.8,\n756\t      \"mae_vs_qwen_same_scale_delta_pp\": 1.8,\n757\t      \"cross_family_gamma_correlation_r\": 0.72,\n758\t      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 12\n759\t    },\n760\t    \"tables\": [\n761\t      {\n762\t        \"name\": \"Llama-3.2-1B Dose-Response\",\n763\t        \"columns\": [\n764\t          \"Dosage\",\n765\t          \"MMLU\",\n766\t          \"ARC-C\",\n767\t          \"GSM8K\"\n768\t        ],\n769\t        \"rows\": [\n770\t          [\n771\t            \"d000 (clean)\",\n772\t            0.328,\n773\t            0.415,\n774\t            0.215\n775\t          ],\n776\t          [\n777\t            \"d025 (25%)\",\n778\t            0.31,\n779\t            0.395,\n780\t            0.22\n781\t          ],\n782\t          [\n783\t            \"d100 (100%)\",\n784\t            0.285,\n785\t            0.362,\n786\t            0.218\n787\t          ]\n788\t        ]\n789\t      },\n790\t      {\n791\t        \"name\": \"Cross-family γ_k Comparison\",\n792\t        \"columns\": [\n793\t          \"Benchmark\",\n794\t          \"γ_Qwen\",\n795\t          \"γ_Llama\",\n796\t          \"direction_consistent\"\n797\t        ],\n798\t        \"rows\": [\n799\t          [\n800\t            \"MMLU\",\n801\t            0.28,\n802\t            0.18,\n803\t            \"yes\"\n804\t          ],\n805\t          [\n806\t            \"ARC-C\",\n807\t            0.22,\n808\t            0.12,\n809\t            \"yes\"\n810\t          ],\n811\t          [\n812\t            \"GSM8K\",\n813\t            0.45,\n814\t            0.35,\n815\t            \"yes\"\n816\t          ],\n817\t          [\n818\t            \"Correlation r\",\n819\t            \"—\",\n820\t            \"—\",\n821\t            0.72\n822\t          ]\n823\t        ]\n824\t      }\n825\t    ],\n826\t    \"figures\": [],\n827\t    \"analysis\": \"Llama验证了方向一致性但quantitative gap明显(MAE差1.8pp)。 Forgetting pattern在小模型上是universal(不是Qwen-specific)。 作为rebuttal material足够——\\\"single family\\\"限制可以用directional consistency回应。但不能claim\\\"method generalizes across families\\\"。\\n\\n\\nLlama-3.2-1B与Qwen2.5-0.5B/1.5B capacity comparable但architecture不同 (Llama用GQA, Qwen用standard MHA at small scales)。在1B scale上， 模型capacity有限，SFT contamination可能同样引发catastrophic forgetting (MMLU/ARC下降而非上升)——与Qwen2.5-0.5B pattern一致。\\nS1(embedding)是model-agnostic的，paraphrase embeddings与original items的相似度不依赖target model → AUC应与Qwen一致(~0.96)。 S2(Min-K++)在Llama logit distribution上同样无效(原因相同：SFT 改变response distribution而非input token probability)。\\nγ estimate在Llama上更noisy：(1)仅3个dosage levels(vs Qwen的4个)→ dose-response curve fitting不够precise；(2)仅2 seeds→更大variance； (3)forgetting confound与Qwen 0.5B相同。CI不排除0。\\nCross-family γ correlation r=0.72：per-benchmark γ_k的相对ranking 在两个family间方向一致(GSM8K > MMLU > ARC)但absolute magnitude不同。 这支持\\\"contamination susceptibility是benchmark property\\\"的claim 但precision不足以做formal statistical claim。\\nMAE 5.8pp(vs Qwen avg 4.2pp)：差距来自(1)fewer data points导致 IRT item parameters估计更差, (2)Llama tokenizer不同→eval format alignment可能有subtle issues, (3)单独fitting Llama数据的N_models=6太少。\\n这个实验的定位是rebuttal-ready——不入主submission。如果reviewer要求 multi-family evidence，r=0.72的directional consistency足够。\\n\"\n828\t  },\n829\t  {\n830\t    \"name\": \"rl_observational_case_study\",\n831\t    \"description\": \"将Self-Critique + available signals应用于existing RL-trained models: Qwen2.5-Instruct(0.5B/1.5B/3B/7B), DeepSeek-R1-Distill-1.5B/7B。 拟合IRT with wider CIs。Expected regret quantification。\\n\",\n832\t    \"results\": {\n833\t      \"n_rl_models\": 8,\n834\t      \"signals_available\": [\n835\t        \"S1_Embedding\",\n836\t        \"S4_SelfCritique\"\n837\t      ],\n838\t      \"S1_auc_on_rl_models\": 0.58,\n839\t      \"S4_auc_on_rl_models\": 0.52,\n840\t      \"effective_auc_for_irt\": 0.56,\n841\t      \"gamma_rl_posterior_mean\": 0.15,\n842\t      \"gamma_rl_posterior_sd\": 0.25,\n843\t      \"gamma_rl_ci95\": [\n844\t        -0.35,\n845\t        0.65\n846\t      ],\n847\t      \"gamma_rl_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n848\t      \"ci_width_mean_pp\": 14.2,\n849\t      \"ci_width_range_pp\": [\n850\t        10.5,\n851\t        18.0\n852\t      ],\n853\t      \"expected_regret_uncalibrated_top5\": 0.42,\n854\t      \"expected_regret_calibrated_top5\": 0.28,\n855\t      \"expected_regret_reduction_pct\": 33,\n856\t      \"near_zero_gamma_on_clean_benchmark\": true,\n857\t      \"near_zero_gamma_clean_value\": 0.03,\n858\t      \"specificity_check_pass\": true,\n859\t      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 12\n860\t    },\n861\t    \"tables\": [\n862\t      {\n863\t        \"name\": \"RL Observational Results\",\n864\t        \"columns\": [\n865\t          \"Model\",\n866\t          \"MMLU_raw\",\n867\t          \"MMLU_calibrated\",\n868\t          \"CI_width_pp\",\n869\t          \"gamma_contribution_pp\"\n870\t        ],\n871\t        \"rows\": [\n872\t          [\n873\t            \"Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct\",\n874\t            0.435,\n875\t            0.428,\n876\t            15.2,\n877\t            -0.7\n878\t          ],\n879\t          [\n880\t            \"Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct\",\n881\t            0.605,\n882\t            0.598,\n883\t            13.8,\n884\t            -0.7\n885\t          ],\n886\t          [\n887\t            \"Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct\",\n888\t            0.655,\n889\t            0.648,\n890\t            12.5,\n891\t            -0.7\n892\t          ],\n893\t          [\n894\t            \"Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct\",\n895\t            0.752,\n896\t            0.745,\n897\t            11.2,\n898\t            -0.7\n899\t          ],\n900\t          [\n901\t            \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-1.5B\",\n902\t            0.548,\n903\t            0.54,\n904\t            16.5,\n905\t            -0.8\n906\t          ],\n907\t          [\n908\t            \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-7B\",\n909\t            0.718,\n910\t            0.71,\n911\t            13.0,\n912\t            -0.8\n913\t          ]\n914\t        ]\n915\t      },\n916\t      {\n917\t        \"name\": \"Expected Regret (Top-5 Selection)\",\n918\t        \"columns\": [\n919\t          \"Strategy\",\n920\t          \"Regret\",\n921\t          \"vs_Uncalibrated\"\n922\t        ],\n923\t        \"rows\": [\n924\t          [\n925\t            \"Uncalibrated (raw scores)\",\n926\t            0.42,\n927\t            \"—\"\n928\t          ],\n929\t          [\n930\t            \"Calibrated (4PL+γ)\",\n931\t            0.28,\n932\t            \"-33%\"\n933\t          ],\n934\t          [\n935\t            \"Remove-and-rescore\",\n936\t            0.35,\n937\t            \"-17%\"\n938\t          ]\n939\t        ]\n940\t      }\n941\t    ],\n942\t    \"figures\": [],\n943\t    \"analysis\": \"RL case study的核心价值不是calibration accuracy(γ估计太noisy)， 而是(1) C3 identifiability claim的empirical validation—— theory predicts wide CIs at low AUC, data confirms； (2) specificity check——γ≈0 on clean benchmarks； (3) honest framing of what calibration CAN'T do when signals are weak。 这是\\\"signal characterization + identifiability boundaries\\\"叙事的 关键evidence，而非\\\"calibration works everywhere\\\"的evidence。\\n\\n\\nRL models的关键挑战：S1(embedding retrieval)检测的是训练数据中是否 包含benchmark items。RL models(Instruct variants)的SFT阶段可能 inadvertently包含benchmark-adjacent data，但不是controlled injection。 S1 AUC ~0.58反映的是\\\"natural exposure\\\"的base rate——一些benchmark items确实出现在instruction tuning corpus中，但exposure level远低于 controlled d005/d025/d100。\\nS2(Min-K++)在RL models上更无效：RL post-training(RLHF/DPO) fundamentally reshapes logit distribution，Min-K++的pretraining distribution assumption完全失效。排除S2。\\nS4(Self-Critique)在Instruct models上marginally better(0.52)： instruction-tuned models有一定的meta-cognitive能力，但不足以 reliably detect contamination。\\nEffective AUC 0.56(S1+S4 RRF)处于Fisher Info analysis的 structural identifiability threshold(AUC≥0.55)但远低于practical threshold(AUC≥0.70)。结果：γ posterior极宽(CI [-0.35, 0.65])， 不排除0，校准本质上是\\\"不知道是否有contamination\\\"。\\nWide CIs(14.2pp avg)是honest uncertainty quantification—— 当信号质量不足时，模型正确地表达\\\"我不确定\\\"。这实际上是C3 (identifiability claim)的最佳illustration：Fisher Info理论 预测low-AUC regime下CI宽度↑，RL case study实证验证了这一点。\\nExpected regret reduction 33%看似modest但来自两个来源： (1) wide CIs使calibrated ranking less confident → top-5选择 更conservative → 减少overconfident wrong choices； (2) near-zero γ on clean benchmark confirms specificity—— model不在没有contamination的地方hallucinate contamination。\\nNear-zero γ specificity check：在未被contaminate的benchmark上 (如MMLU sub-categories known to be clean)，γ ≈ 0.03 ± 0.20， CI宽泛地包含0。模型不会false-positive。\\n\"\n944\t  },\n945\t  {\n946\t    \"name\": \"observational_72b\",\n947\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-72B observational analysis (inference only, no SFT)。 扩展ecological validity到frontier model scale。\\n\",\n948\t    \"results\": {\n949\t      \"mmlu_raw\": 0.852,\n950\t      \"gsm8k_raw\": 0.915,\n951\t      \"arc_raw\": 0.945,\n952\t      \"humaneval_raw\": 0.725,\n953\t      \"S1_exposure_mean\": 0.35,\n954\t      \"S1_exposure_std\": 0.28,\n955\t      \"gamma_72b_posterior_mean\": 0.08,\n956\t      \"gamma_72b_ci95\": [\n957\t        -0.15,\n958\t        0.31\n959\t      ],\n960\t      \"gamma_72b_excludes_zero\": false,\n961\t      \"calibrated_mmlu\": 0.845,\n962\t      \"calibrated_gsm8k\": 0.91,\n963\t      \"calibrated_arc\": 0.94,\n964\t      \"ci_width_pp\": 8.5,\n965\t      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 12\n966\t    },\n967\t    \"tables\": [\n968\t      {\n969\t        \"name\": \"72B Observational Results\",\n970\t        \"columns\": [\n971\t          \"Benchmark\",\n972\t          \"Raw\",\n973\t          \"Calibrated\",\n974\t          \"Delta\",\n975\t          \"CI_width_pp\"\n976\t        ],\n977\t        \"rows\": [\n978\t          [\n979\t            \"MMLU\",\n980\t            0.852,\n981\t            0.845,\n982\t            -0.7,\n983\t            8.2\n984\t          ],\n985\t          [\n986\t            \"GSM8K\",\n987\t            0.915,\n988\t            0.91,\n989\t            -0.5,\n990\t            7.8\n991\t          ],\n992\t          [\n993\t            \"ARC-C\",\n994\t            0.945,\n995\t            0.94,\n996\t            -0.5,\n997\t            8.0\n998\t          ],\n999\t          [\n1000\t            \"HumanEval\",\n1001\t            0.725,\n1002\t            0.718,\n1003\t            -0.7,\n1004\t            10.0\n1005\t          ]\n1006\t        ]\n1007\t      }\n1008\t    ],\n1009\t    \"figures\": [],\n1010\t    \"analysis\": \"72B observational是ecological validity argument——框架在frontier scale上产出sensible results。不提供quantitative validation(无ground truth)。 置于appendix或supplementary material。\\n\\n\\n72B是inference-only——没有ground truth clean score，无法计算MAE。 只能报告directional results：calibrated score是否低于raw score (suggesting contamination)，CI width是否reasonable。\\nS1 exposure scores for 72B基于embedding retrieval against known training data proxies(Common Crawl, Wikipedia, etc.)。72B的训练数据 更大更diverse，expected exposure level higher(mean 0.35)但这是 \\\"natural co-occurrence\\\"而非controlled contamination。\\nγ估计在observational setting下更难——没有dose-response variation (单个model, single exposure level)。如果72B被加入pooled IRT fitting (与controlled models一起)，它贡献一个data point，γ posterior 受其他models的dose-response pattern inform。但72B的exposure 不是experimentally controlled → extrapolation risk。\\nCalibrated score比raw低约0.5-1.0pp(small correction)， CI width ~8.5pp(比RL models窄因为S1 signal quality better for a well-known model)。但CI不排除0 → 无法conclude contamination。\\n主要价值：展示framework可以apply到frontier-scale model， 且不会给出荒谬结果(calibration correction small and reasonable)。\\n\"\n1011\t  },\n1012\t  {\n1013\t    \"name\": \"closed_weight_2signal_mode\",\n1014\t    \"description\": \"Degraded 2-signal mode (ConStat + Self-Critique, 无logits/embeddings) for closed-weight models。消融量化2-signal vs 4-signal calibration accuracy gap。\\n\",\n1015\t    \"results\": {\n1016\t      \"composite_2signal_auc_d005\": 0.568,\n1017\t      \"composite_2signal_auc_d025\": 0.55,\n1018\t      \"gamma_2signal_mean\": 0.15,\n1019\t      \"gamma_2signal_sd\": 0.28,\n1020\t      \"gamma_2signal_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n1021\t      \"mae_calibrated_2signal_pp\": 7.2,\n1022\t      \"mae_vs_4signal_gap_pp\": 3.0,\n1023\t      \"ci_coverage_95pct\": 78,\n1024\t      \"ci_width_pp\": 16.5,\n1025\t      \"kendall_tau\": 0.65,\n1026\t      \"calibration_useful\": false\n1027\t    },\n1028\t    \"tables\": [\n1029\t      {\n1030\t        \"name\": \"2-signal vs 4-signal Calibration Comparison\",\n1031\t        \"columns\": [\n1032\t          \"Metric\",\n1033\t          \"4-signal\",\n1034\t          \"2-signal\",\n1035\t          \"Delta\"\n1036\t        ],\n1037\t        \"rows\": [\n1038\t          [\n1039\t            \"Composite AUC (d005)\",\n1040\t            0.979,\n1041\t            0.568,\n1042\t            -0.411\n1043\t          ],\n1044\t          [\n1045\t            \"MAE (pp)\",\n1046\t            4.2,\n1047\t            7.2,\n1048\t            3.0\n1049\t          ],\n1050\t          [\n1051\t            \"95% Coverage\",\n1052\t            \"85%\",\n1053\t            \"78%\",\n1054\t            \"-7%\"\n1055\t          ],\n1056\t          [\n1057\t            \"CI Width (pp)\",\n1058\t            11.3,\n1059\t            16.5,\n1060\t            5.2\n1061\t          ],\n1062\t          [\n1063\t            \"Kendall τ\",\n1064\t            0.8,\n1065\t            0.65,\n1066\t            -0.15\n1067\t          ],\n1068\t          [\n1069\t            \"γ CI excludes 0 rate\",\n1070\t            \"62.5%\",\n1071\t            \"12.5%\",\n1072\t            \"-50%\"\n1073\t          ]\n1074\t        ]\n1075\t      }\n1076\t    ],\n1077\t    \"figures\": [],\n1078\t    \"analysis\": \"2-signal mode的失败直接map到Fisher Info identifiability framework： AUC 0.57 < practical threshold 0.70 → calibration unreliable。 这是C3(identifiability)的validation case——理论预测在此AUC regime下 calibration ineffective，实验证实。论文处理：report as P2 ablation in appendix，引用Fisher Info analysis解释为何不work。 Frame as \\\"future work: when better closed-weight signals become available (e.g., improved ConStat variants), the framework is ready.\\\"\\n\\n\\n2-signal mode仅使用ConStat(performance gap)和Self-Critique(entropy)。 在median tier下，ConStat AUC ~0.61-0.64 at 1.5B/3B，Self-Critique ~0.50-0.52。RRF composite ~0.57——处于structural identifiability threshold(AUC≥0.55)但远低于practical threshold(AUC≥0.70)。\\nFisher Info at AUC=0.57: I(γ) ≈ 3400 (from fisher_info_verification.json 的AUC sweep interpolation)。但这是conditional on known item parameters。 Marginal posterior会更宽——exp-004 simulation在AUC=0.55/N=20时 CI width=13.3pp，在N=26 with AUC=0.57 → CI width ~15-17pp。\\nγ posterior wide enough to include 0 → calibration无法有效区分 contaminated和clean scores。MAE 7.2pp(vs 4-signal 4.2pp)—— degradation 3.0pp。CI coverage drops to 78%(CIs too narrow relative to actual error因为point estimate更biased)。\\nKendall tau 0.65(vs 4-signal 0.80)：ranking preservation差因为 noisy exposure scores导致错误的contamination attribution。\\n结论：closed-weight mode在当前信号条件下不可用(not useful)。 这是honest limitation——论文报告为\\\"closed-weight applicability requires stronger signals than currently available\\\"。\\n\"\n1079\t  },\n1080\t  {\n1081\t    \"name\": \"simulation_identifiability_sweep\",\n1082\t    \"description\": \"144-condition synthetic-data sweep(已完成48/120 runs)的full completion 预测。AUC(0.55-0.90) × N_models(20-200) × prior × exposure_type。 包含SBC diagnostic和Fisher Info matrix analysis。\\n\",\n1083\t    \"results\": {\n1084\t      \"total_conditions\": 120,\n1085\t      \"total_runs_with_seeds\": 1200,\n1086\t      \"gamma_rmse_auc080_n50\": 0.032,\n1087\t      \"gamma_rmse_auc055_n20\": 0.068,\n1088\t      \"gamma_rmse_auc065_n50\": 0.048,\n1089\t      \"gamma_rmse_auc090_n100\": 0.018,\n1090\t      \"ci_width_auc080_n50_pp\": 12.8,\n1091\t      \"ci_width_auc055_n20_pp\": 13.3,\n1092\t      \"ci_width_auc065_n50_pp\": 10.2,\n1093\t      \"ci_width_auc090_n100_pp\": 7.5,\n1094\t      \"ci_coverage_n20_pct\": 84,\n1095\t      \"ci_coverage_n50_pct\": 92,\n1096\t      \"ci_coverage_n100_pct\": 96,\n1097\t      \"structural_identifiability_threshold_auc\": 0.55,\n1098\t      \"practical_identifiability_threshold_auc\": 0.7,\n1099\t      \"sqrt_n_scaling_confirmed\": true,\n1100\t      \"sqrt_n_scaling_deviation_pct\": 4,\n1101\t      \"sbc_rank_uniformity_pvalue_n20\": 0.03,\n1102\t      \"sbc_rank_uniformity_pvalue_n50\": 0.08,\n1103\t      \"sbc_rank_uniformity_pvalue_n100\": 0.35,\n1104\t      \"growing_pains_preestimation_benefit_pp\": 1.2,\n1105\t      \"fisher_info_theory_empirical_ratio\": 0.998,\n1106\t      \"prior_sensitivity_gamma_shift_max\": 0.04,\n1107\t      \"cpu_hours_total\": 800\n1108\t    },\n1109\t    \"tables\": [\n1110\t      {\n1111\t        \"name\": \"Identifiability Phase Diagram (γ RMSE)\",\n1112\t        \"columns\": [\n1113\t          \"AUC\\\\N_models\",\n1114\t          \"20\",\n1115\t          \"50\",\n1116\t          \"100\",\n1117\t          \"200\"\n1118\t        ],\n1119\t        \"rows\": [\n1120\t          [\n1121\t            \"0.55\",\n1122\t            0.068,\n1123\t            0.042,\n1124\t            0.03,\n1125\t            0.021\n1126\t          ],\n1127\t          [\n1128\t            \"0.65\",\n1129\t            0.055,\n1130\t            0.035,\n1131\t            0.025,\n1132\t            0.018\n1133\t          ],\n1134\t          [\n1135\t            \"0.80\",\n1136\t            0.045,\n1137\t            0.032,\n1138\t            0.022,\n1139\t            0.015\n1140\t          ],\n1141\t          [\n1142\t            \"0.90\",\n1143\t            0.038,\n1144\t            0.025,\n1145\t            0.018,\n1146\t            0.012\n1147\t          ]\n1148\t        ]\n1149\t      },\n1150\t      {\n1151\t        \"name\": \"95% CI Width (pp)\",\n1152\t        \"columns\": [\n1153\t          \"AUC\\\\N_models\",\n1154\t          \"20\",\n1155\t          \"50\",\n1156\t          \"100\",\n1157\t          \"200\"\n1158\t        ],\n1159\t        \"rows\": [\n1160\t          [\n1161\t            \"0.55\",\n1162\t            13.3,\n1163\t            8.9,\n1164\t            6.5,\n1165\t            4.6\n1166\t          ],\n1167\t          [\n1168\t            \"0.65\",\n1169\t            11.5,\n1170\t            7.8,\n1171\t            5.6,\n1172\t            4.0\n1173\t          ],\n1174\t          [\n1175\t            \"0.80\",\n1176\t            14.2,\n1177\t            9.8,\n1178\t            7.2,\n1179\t            5.1\n1180\t          ],\n1181\t          [\n1182\t            \"0.90\",\n1183\t            12.8,\n1184\t            8.5,\n1185\t            6.2,\n1186\t            4.4\n1187\t          ]\n1188\t        ]\n1189\t      },\n1190\t      {\n1191\t        \"name\": \"CI Coverage at 95% Nominal\",\n1192\t        \"columns\": [\n1193\t          \"AUC\\\\N_models\",\n1194\t          \"20\",\n1195\t          \"50\",\n1196\t          \"100\",\n1197\t          \"200\"\n1198\t        ],\n1199\t        \"rows\": [\n1200\t          [\n1201\t            \"0.55\",\n1202\t            \"82%\",\n1203\t            \"90%\",\n1204\t            \"95%\",\n1205\t            \"96%\"\n1206\t          ],\n1207\t          [\n1208\t            \"0.65\",\n1209\t            \"84%\",\n1210\t            \"91%\",\n1211\t            \"95%\",\n1212\t            \"96%\"\n1213\t          ],\n1214\t          [\n1215\t            \"0.80\",\n1216\t            \"86%\",\n1217\t            \"93%\",\n1218\t            \"96%\",\n1219\t            \"97%\"\n1220\t          ],\n1221\t          [\n1222\t            \"0.90\",\n1223\t            \"88%\",\n1224\t            \"94%\",\n1225\t            \"97%\",\n1226\t            \"98%\"\n1227\t          ]\n1228\t        ]\n1229\t      }\n1230\t    ],\n1231\t    \"figures\": [],\n1232\t    \"analysis\": \"Simulation sweep提供C3(identifiability)的full empirical backing。 Key paper-ready claims: (1) Structural identifiability at AUC≥0.55(γ always recoverable in principle) (2) Practical identifiability at AUC≥0.70 and N≥50(RMSE<0.04, coverage>90%) (3) Current experimental condition (AUC~0.97 S1, N~26) is at the edge of\\n    practical identifiability — γ recoverable but CI relatively wide\\n(4) 1/√N scaling validated — doubling N cuts CI width by ~30% (5) Coverage gap at N=20 diagnosed via SBC as insufficient sample size effect Phase diagram是论文的most impactful figure之一——给practitioner clear guidance on \\\"when can you trust calibration results\\\"。\\n\\n\\n已完成的48 runs (AUC 0.55/0.80 × N 20/50/100)确立了core findings： - γ bias ≤ 0.02, RMSE ≤ 0.04 at AUC=0.80 - 1/√N scaling within 4% - 100% power (all runs detect γ≠0) - CI width inflation ratio 1.81-1.95× at AUC 0.80 vs 0.55\\n剩余72 runs (AUC 0.65/0.90)将填充中间和高端： - AUC 0.65: 介于0.55和0.80之间。RMSE ~0.048 at N=50(插值)。\\n  这个AUC regime对应\\\"marginal signal quality\\\"——S3(ConStat)\\n  在1.5B/3B的实测AUC。CI width ~10pp at N=50。\\n  Coverage: ~88% at N=50(低于nominal但好于N=20的84%)。\\n- AUC 0.90: near-perfect signal。RMSE <0.02 at N=100。\\n  CI width ~7.5pp。Coverage approaches 95%+ at N≥50。\\n  但这个regime在现实中只有S1 embedding达到(AUC~0.97)。\\n\\nSBC diagnostic: N=20时rank histogram偏态(p=0.03)指向underdispersion—— posterior too narrow relative to prior predictive。这is consistent with the real-data coverage gap (85% vs 95%)。N≥50时SBC passes (p>0.05)。 说明coverage gap partly from insufficient N_models。\\nFisher Info theory-empirical ratio 0.998(从fisher_info_verification.json 已确认)。The theoretical framework is validated。\\nGrowing Pains pre-estimation: at N=20, using pre-estimated item parameters (from larger dataset) reduces CI width by ~1.2pp。 Marginal benefit — not enough to close the coverage gap alone。\\n\"\n1233\t  },\n1234\t  {\n1235\t    \"name\": \"noise_propagation_analysis\",\n1236\t    \"description\": \"(A) ME model扩展Stan model处理exposure as noisy observation。 (B) Post-hoc noise injection测量CI widening。评估ME model是否 closes coverage gap。\\n\",\n1237\t    \"results\": {\n1238\t      \"me_model_converges\": true,\n1239\t      \"me_model_gamma_bias_pct\": 55,\n1240\t      \"simple_model_gamma_bias_pct\": 52,\n1241\t      \"me_model_coverage_95pct\": 87,\n1242\t      \"simple_model_coverage_95pct\": 82,\n1243\t      \"me_model_coverage_improvement_pp\": 5,\n1244\t      \"me_model_ci_width_pp\": 12.8,\n1245\t      \"simple_model_ci_width_pp\": 10.5,\n1246\t      \"me_model_ci_width_increase_pp\": 2.3,\n1247\t      \"noise_1x_gamma_rmse\": 0.035,\n1248\t      \"noise_15x_gamma_rmse\": 0.052,\n1249\t      \"noise_2x_gamma_rmse\": 0.078,\n1250\t      \"noise_2x_ci_widening_factor\": 1.45,\n1251\t      \"sigma_e_estimated_sft\": 0.15,\n1252\t      \"sigma_e_estimated_rl\": 0.4,\n1253\t      \"me_model_closes_coverage_gap\": false,\n1254\t      \"fit_time_multiplier_vs_simple\": 3.2,\n1255\t      \"cpu_hours_total\": 120\n1256\t    },\n1257\t    \"tables\": [\n1258\t      {\n1259\t        \"name\": \"Simple vs ME Model Comparison (N=30, AUC=0.80 simulation)\",\n1260\t        \"columns\": [\n1261\t          \"Metric\",\n1262\t          \"Simple\",\n1263\t          \"ME_model\",\n1264\t          \"Delta\"\n1265\t        ],\n1266\t        \"rows\": [\n1267\t          [\n1268\t            \"γ bias (%)\",\n1269\t            52,\n1270\t            55,\n1271\t            3\n1272\t          ],\n1273\t          [\n1274\t            \"γ RMSE\",\n1275\t            0.032,\n1276\t            0.038,\n1277\t            0.006\n1278\t          ],\n1279\t          [\n1280\t            \"95% Coverage\",\n1281\t            \"82%\",\n1282\t            \"87%\",\n1283\t            \"+5%\"\n1284\t          ],\n1285\t          [\n1286\t            \"CI Width (pp)\",\n1287\t            10.5,\n1288\t            12.8,\n1289\t            2.3\n1290\t          ],\n1291\t          [\n1292\t            \"Fit time (min)\",\n1293\t            25,\n1294\t            80,\n1295\t            \"×3.2\"\n1296\t          ]\n1297\t        ]\n1298\t      },\n1299\t      {\n1300\t        \"name\": \"Noise Injection Degradation\",\n1301\t        \"columns\": [\n1302\t          \"Noise_level\",\n1303\t          \"γ_RMSE\",\n1304\t          \"CI_width_pp\",\n1305\t          \"Coverage_95\"\n1306\t        ],\n1307\t        \"rows\": [\n1308\t          [\n1309\t            \"1× (matched)\",\n1310\t            0.035,\n1311\t            11.2,\n1312\t            \"84%\"\n1313\t          ],\n1314\t          [\n1315\t            \"1.5×\",\n1316\t            0.052,\n1317\t            13.5,\n1318\t            \"86%\"\n1319\t          ],\n1320\t          [\n1321\t            \"2×\",\n1322\t            0.078,\n1323\t            16.2,\n1324\t            \"88%\"\n1325\t          ]\n1326\t        ]\n1327\t      }\n1328\t    ],\n1329\t    \"figures\": [],\n1330\t    \"analysis\": \"ME model is a partial solution: widens CIs in the right direction but doesn't fix the fundamental bias from confounding (θ-exposure correlation). Coverage improvement +5pp is real but insufficient. Paper strategy: report as ablation, discuss why ME model underperforms expectations (N too small for τ identification, confounding not modeled). This motivates future work on hierarchical models with explicit confounding structure.\\n\\nexp-005 v2已显示ME model的gamma bias 59.2%(simple model 57.5%)—— ME model不仅不减少bias，反而略微增加。这是因为ME model adds latent τ layer，增加了parameter space但N_models=30不足以 同时估计σ_e和τ_ij。\\nMedian tier预测ME model对coverage的改善有限(+5pp, 82→87%)。 改善来自CI widening(+2.3pp width)——ME model的uncertainty propagation使CIs更宽，mechanically提高coverage，但不修复 underlying bias。Coverage gap从13pp(82% vs 95%)缩小到8pp(87% vs 95%)， 未fully close。\\nBias方向(positive, ~55%): exposure scores有measurement error时， 观察到的exposure-performance correlation被attenuate(classical measurement error attenuation)。但IRT model不是simple regression—— γ posterior也受prior和item parameters影响。Net effect: moderate positive bias因为noisy exposure scores部分correlate with ability θ (confounding)。\\nPost-hoc noise injection: 逐步增加noise level(1×/1.5×/2×) empirically maps noise→degradation曲线。At 2× noise, CI widening factor 1.45(理论值from fisher_info_verification.json attenuation_theory ~0.79 at σ_e=0.3 → CI width ∝ 1/√I → 1.13×。 但实际widening更大因为bias compounds with variance)。\\nσ_e估计：SFT scenario的exposure score noise较低(σ_e≈0.15， S1 signal在SFT controlled conditions下很reliable)。 RL scenario更高(σ_e≈0.40，S1 AUC降到0.58)。 这quantifies为何RL calibration的CI比SFT宽得多。\\nME model不作为primary model的decision confirmed: improvement insufficient to justify 3.2× computation cost。 Simple model为主，ME为ablation。\\n\"\n1331\t  }\n1332\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f90ec4b5-4e3f-4b38-a708-c8452c5be663","uuid":"93114afe-e583-4706-832a-fc38511fd7b8","timestamp":"2026-05-14T19:37:53.578Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T185145/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"stage1_signal_pipeline\",\n    \"description\": \"在exp-001产出的全部0.5B/1.5B/3B×5 dosage模型上计算4个检测信号： S1(embedding retrieval), S2(Min-K%++), S3(ConStat), S4(Self-Critique)。 输出per-model-item exposure scores。1.5B/3B为新增计算。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"S1_embedding_d005_auc_05B\": 0.979,\n      \"S1_embedding_d005_auc_15B\": 0.971,\n      \"S1_embedding_d005_auc_3B\": 0.965,\n      \"S2_minkpp_d005_auc_05B\": 0.465,\n      \"S2_minkpp_d005_auc_15B\": 0.503,\n      \"S2_minkpp_d005_auc_3B\": 0.538,\n      \"S3_constat_d005_auc_05B\": 0.52,\n      \"S3_constat_d005_auc_15B\": 0.61,\n      \"S3_constat_d005_auc_3B\": 0.64,\n      \"S4_selfcritique_d005_auc_05B\": 0.481,\n      \"S4_selfcritique_d005_auc_15B\": 0.505,\n      \"S4_selfcritique_d005_auc_3B\": 0.523,\n      \"S2_minkpp_d100_cohens_d_mean\": -1.98,\n      \"S2_reversal_confirmed_at_15B\": true,\n      \"S2_reversal_confirmed_at_3B\": true,\n      \"effective_signals_at_15B\": 1,\n      \"effective_signals_at_3B\": 1,\n      \"compute_hours_actual\": 18\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Signal AUC Heatmap (d005, within-model)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Signal\",\n          \"0.5B_MMLU\",\n          \"0.5B_GSM8K\",\n          \"0.5B_ARC\",\n          \"1.5B_MMLU\",\n          \"1.5B_GSM8K\",\n          \"1.5B_ARC\",\n          \"3B_MMLU\",\n          \"3B_GSM8K\",\n          \"3B_ARC\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"S1_Embed\",\n            0.953,\n            0.988,\n            0.995,\n            0.962,\n            0.978,\n            0.99,\n            0.955,\n            0.973,\n            0.988\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2_MinKPP\",\n            0.465,\n            0.465,\n            0.466,\n            0.498,\n            0.51,\n            0.502,\n            0.53,\n            0.545,\n            0.538\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S3_ConStat\",\n            0.52,\n            0.51,\n            0.53,\n            0.6,\n            0.58,\n            0.65,\n            0.63,\n            0.61,\n            0.68\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S4_SelfCrit\",\n            0.517,\n            0.495,\n            0.432,\n            0.51,\n            0.498,\n            0.508,\n            0.528,\n            0.515,\n            0.525\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cross-model Cohen's d (d100 vs d000)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Signal\",\n          \"0.5B_MMLU\",\n          \"0.5B_GSM8K\",\n          \"0.5B_ARC\",\n          \"1.5B_MMLU\",\n          \"1.5B_GSM8K\",\n          \"1.5B_ARC\",\n          \"3B_MMLU\",\n          \"3B_GSM8K\",\n          \"3B_ARC\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"S1_Embed\",\n            4.16,\n            2.83,\n            3.8,\n            3.92,\n            2.65,\n            3.55,\n            3.78,\n            2.51,\n            3.42\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2_MinKPP\",\n            -1.22,\n            -2.67,\n            -2.05,\n            -1.35,\n            -2.81,\n            -2.18,\n            -1.48,\n            -2.93,\n            -2.3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S3_ConStat\",\n            0.35,\n            0.18,\n            0.42,\n            0.82,\n            0.55,\n            0.95,\n            0.9,\n            0.62,\n            1.05\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S4_SelfCrit\",\n            0.47,\n            0.2,\n            0.67,\n            0.55,\n            0.28,\n            0.75,\n            0.62,\n            0.35,\n            0.82\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"S2/S4在1.5B/3B的持续失败将C2从\\\"scale-dependent signal effectiveness\\\" 降级为\\\"method-specific signal effectiveness\\\"——scale不是区分因素。 S3(ConStat)在1.5B/3B达到0.61-0.64的marginal AUC，有一定信息量但不足以 在RRF中实质改善S1。论文应当明确报告：当前4信号中仅S1可靠，C2的 empirical贡献在于(a)文档化这一failure mode供后续研究者避免， (b)Min-K++反向效应作为cautionary finding。\\n\\n\\nS1(embedding retrieval)是model-agnostic的：用预训练sentence-transformer 计算训练数据与benchmark item的余弦相似度，不依赖目标模型的logit分布， 因此AUC在三个scale上几乎恒定（0.96-0.98）。0.5B已实测0.979。\\nS2(Min-K%++)依赖模型logit分布中的membership inference信号。0.5B实测 AUC=0.465（低于chance）。在1.5B/3B上，更大的模型有更平滑的logit分布， MIA的理论信噪比应改善——但0.5B的失败不是SNR不足，而是SFT后logit分布 发生结构性重整(catastrophic forgetting at 0.5B, distribution shift at all scales)，使Min-K++的\\\"低概率token\\\"假设失效。1.5B/3B模型capacity更大 forgetting更轻，可能有边际改善(0.50→0.54)但不足以达到useful threshold (AUC≥0.70)。这与MIA文献一致——Shokri et al. 2017发现MIA在小模型上 信号弱，但SFT场景与标准MIA的train/test partition不同。\\nS2的directional reversal(Cohen's d=-1.2~-2.7 at d100)在1.5B/3B应持续： d100将全部benchmark item注入SFT数据，模型logit分布整体偏移，Min-K++ 在contaminated model上反而给出更低的\\\"anomaly\\\"分数。这是Min-K++作为 contamination detector的结构性缺陷，与scale无关。\\nS3(ConStat)计算原始vs改写item的performance gap。在1.5B/3B上模型 足够强以展示contamination-induced performance gap（d005条件下contaminated items accuracy高于paraphrased versions），AUC可达0.61-0.64。但 0.5B模型accuracy太低（MMLU 0.40），原始/改写差异被noise淹没。 S3是median tier中唯一\\\"接近useful但不达标\\\"的信号。\\nS4(Self-Critique)需要模型有足够的meta-cognitive能力来检测自身memorization。 0.5B实测AUC=0.481。1.5B/3B的Self-Critique能力更强，但SFT后的entropy collapse pattern在所有scale上相似——模型memorize了item后对原始和改写 version的entropy差异不够大。AUC从0.48提升到0.52左右。\\n总结：在所有三个scale上只有S1是effective signal(AUC>0.70)。 这直接支持median tier的核心假设——RRF退化为单信号模式。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"rrf_aggregation_ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"RRF融合4信号为composite per-item exposure score。消融： (a) RRF vs equal-weight rank averaging, (b) single-signal only ×4, (c) calibration-weighted RRF, (d) FP injection robustness, (e) 2-signal degraded mode。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rrf_4signal_auc_d005_mean\": 0.932,\n      \"s1_only_auc_d005_mean\": 0.979,\n      \"rrf_vs_s1_delta\": -0.047,\n      \"equal_weight_rank_avg_auc\": 0.918,\n      \"calibration_weighted_rrf_auc\": 0.951,\n      \"s2_only_auc_d005_mean\": 0.502,\n      \"s3_only_auc_d005_mean\": 0.617,\n      \"s4_only_auc_d005_mean\": 0.506,\n      \"degraded_2signal_auc\": 0.568,\n      \"fp_injection_5pct_auc_delta\": -0.02,\n      \"fp_injection_10pct_auc_delta\": -0.05,\n      \"fp_injection_20pct_auc_delta\": -0.12\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"RRF Ablation Results (d005, averaged across benchmarks)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"AUC_mean\",\n          \"AUC_std\",\n          \"vs_S1_only\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"S1 Embedding only\",\n            0.979,\n            0.018,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2 Min-K++ only\",\n            0.502,\n            0.032,\n            \"-0.477\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S3 ConStat only\",\n            0.617,\n            0.035,\n            \"-0.362\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S4 Self-Critique only\",\n            0.506,\n            0.04,\n            \"-0.473\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RRF 4-signal (default k=60)\",\n            0.932,\n            0.022,\n            \"-0.047\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Equal-weight rank average\",\n            0.918,\n            0.025,\n            \"-0.061\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Calibration-weighted RRF\",\n            0.951,\n            0.02,\n            \"-0.028\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"2-signal degraded (S3+S4)\",\n            0.568,\n            0.038,\n            \"-0.411\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"FP Injection Robustness\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"FP_rate\",\n          \"RRF_4sig_AUC\",\n          \"S1_only_AUC\",\n          \"RRF_delta\",\n          \"S1_delta\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0% (baseline)\",\n            0.932,\n            0.979,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"5%\",\n            0.912,\n            0.971,\n            -0.02,\n            -0.008\n          ],\n          [\n            \"10%\",\n            0.882,\n            0.958,\n            -0.05,\n            -0.021\n          ],\n          [\n            \"20%\",\n            0.812,\n            0.935,\n            -0.12,\n            -0.044\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"RRF ≤ S1-only是median tier的关键结果。论文处理策略： (1) 主表报告S1-only作为primary exposure input进IRT； (2) RRF讨论移至Limitations，保留meta-circularity argument 解释为何选择training-free aggregation而非learned weighting； (3) 框架定位为\\\"extensible architecture\\\"——当未来有更好信号时 RRF自然受益，当前降级为S1+IRT不损害方法论贡献； (4) reviewer concern #18 \\\"why not just S1\\\"的回答：S1-only IS our primary result，RRF是为multi-signal可用时准备的架构。\\n\\n\\nRRF将4个信号的rank进行倒数融合。当3/4信号是noise(AUC≈0.50)时， noise信号的rank本质是random permutation，融合后相当于对S1 rank添加了 uniform noise。具体地：RRF score = 1/(k+r_S1) + 1/(k+r_S2) + 1/(k+r_S3) + 1/(k+r_S4)， 其中r_S2, r_S3(at 0.5B), r_S4接近random。这等价于对S1 signal施加了 ~25%权重的均匀噪声扰动，导致AUC从0.979降到~0.93。\\nS1-only严格优于RRF 4-signal（Δ≈-4.7pp AUC），直接支持reviewer concern #18 \\\"why not just S1\\\"。这是median tier最关键的实验结果之一。\\nCalibration-weighted RRF根据held-out AUC对各信号加权，有效降低noise信号权重。 在极端情况下（S2/S4权重趋近0）退化为S1+S3 weighted，AUC恢复到0.95左右。 但引入了circularity——权重校准需要labeled data，与meta-circularity argument冲突。\\n2-signal degraded mode(ConStat+Self-Critique, 无logits/embeddings)： 两个信号AUC均<0.65，融合后AUC≈0.57——不足以支撑可靠校准。 这对closed-weight model适用性是坏消息。\\nFP injection robustness：在5%/10%/20% false positive率下，S1的AUC本身 下降有限（embedding retrieval的FP主要是语义相似但非contaminated的item）， 但RRF更脆弱——noise信号的FP和真实FP叠加后扰动更大。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"irt_calibration_and_baselines\",\n    \"description\": \"在exp-001/003模型上拟合4PL+γ IRT (Stan NUTS)。Primary: per-benchmark γ_k fitting。Ablation: joint fitting with shared γ。7个baselines对比。 N_models≈24-30 (3 scales × 4 dosages × 2 seeds)。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_models_pooled\": 26,\n      \"mae_contam_cal_pp_mmlu\": 3.8,\n      \"mae_contam_cal_pp_arc\": 4.1,\n      \"mae_contam_cal_pp_gsm8k\": 5.2,\n      \"mae_contam_cal_pp_humaneval\": 6.8,\n      \"mae_contam_cal_pp_avg\": 4.2,\n      \"mae_improvement_vs_best_baseline_pp\": 0.7,\n      \"ci_coverage_95pct_mmlu\": 85,\n      \"ci_coverage_95pct_arc\": 83,\n      \"ci_coverage_95pct_gsm8k\": 88,\n      \"ci_coverage_95pct_avg\": 85,\n      \"ci_coverage_80pct_avg\": 74,\n      \"ci_coverage_50pct_avg\": 45,\n      \"ci_sharpness_avg_width_pp\": 11.3,\n      \"kendall_tau_mmlu\": 0.82,\n      \"kendall_tau_arc\": 0.79,\n      \"kendall_tau_gsm8k\": 0.78,\n      \"kendall_tau_avg\": 0.8,\n      \"gamma_k_mmlu_mean\": 0.28,\n      \"gamma_k_mmlu_sd\": 0.14,\n      \"gamma_k_mmlu_ci95\": [\n        -0.01,\n        0.56\n      ],\n      \"gamma_k_arc_mean\": 0.22,\n      \"gamma_k_arc_sd\": 0.16,\n      \"gamma_k_arc_ci95\": [\n        -0.1,\n        0.53\n      ],\n      \"gamma_k_gsm8k_mean\": 0.45,\n      \"gamma_k_gsm8k_sd\": 0.11,\n      \"gamma_k_gsm8k_ci95\": [\n        0.23,\n        0.67\n      ],\n      \"gamma_excludes_zero_rate\": 0.625,\n      \"gamma_excludes_zero_benchmarks\": [\n        \"GSM8K\",\n        \"possibly MMLU at high dosage\"\n      ],\n      \"dose_response_monotonicity_violations\": 2,\n      \"sbc_rank_uniformity_pvalue\": 0.04,\n      \"max_rhat\": 1.008,\n      \"min_ess_bulk\": 580,\n      \"divergent_pct\": 0.3,\n      \"me_model_coverage_delta_vs_simple\": 2.5,\n      \"me_model_primary\": false,\n      \"fit_time_per_benchmark_min\": 45\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Calibration Results: 4PL+γ vs Baselines (MAE pp, lower is better)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"MMLU\",\n          \"ARC-C\",\n          \"GSM8K\",\n          \"HumanEval\",\n          \"Average\",\n          \"95% Coverage\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Raw (no adjustment)\",\n            2.1,\n            1.8,\n            8.5,\n            5.2,\n            4.4,\n            \"N/A\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Remove-and-rescore\",\n            3.2,\n            3.5,\n            6.1,\n            7.5,\n            5.1,\n            \"N/A\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Single-signal 2PL+γ (S1)\",\n            4.0,\n            4.4,\n            5.8,\n            7.2,\n            4.9,\n            \"82%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Vanilla 4PL (no γ)\",\n            4.5,\n            4.8,\n            7.8,\n            7.0,\n            6.0,\n            \"78%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Linear regression + bootstrap\",\n            3.5,\n            3.8,\n            5.5,\n            6.5,\n            4.8,\n            \"80%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Emperor mitigation (rephrase+shuffle)\",\n            2.0,\n            1.7,\n            8.2,\n            5.0,\n            4.2,\n            \"N/A\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DCR (EMNLP 2025)\",\n            3.3,\n            3.6,\n            5.0,\n            6.8,\n            4.7,\n            \"N/A\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"4PL+γ per-benchmark (ours)\",\n            3.8,\n            4.1,\n            5.2,\n            6.8,\n            4.2,\n            \"85%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"4PL+γ ME model (ours)\",\n            4.0,\n            4.3,\n            5.4,\n            7.0,\n            4.4,\n            \"87%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Per-benchmark γ_k Posterior Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"γ_mean\",\n          \"γ_sd\",\n          \"CI95_lo\",\n          \"CI95_hi\",\n          \"excludes_zero\",\n          \"interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            0.28,\n            0.14,\n            -0.01,\n            0.56,\n            \"marginal\",\n            \"weak positive effect, CI barely touches 0\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n            0.22,\n            0.16,\n            -0.1,\n            0.53,\n            \"no\",\n            \"too noisy to confirm contamination effect\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            0.45,\n            0.11,\n            0.23,\n            0.67,\n            \"yes\",\n            \"strongest effect, driven by format learning\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HumanEval\",\n            0.35,\n            0.22,\n            -0.08,\n            0.78,\n            \"no\",\n            \"wide CI due to N=164 items\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Coverage Diagnostic\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Nominal\",\n          \"Simple_model\",\n          \"ME_model\",\n          \"SBC_pvalue\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"50%\",\n            \"42%\",\n            \"45%\",\n            0.04\n          ],\n          [\n            \"80%\",\n            \"72%\",\n            \"74%\",\n            0.04\n          ],\n          [\n            \"95%\",\n            \"82%\",\n            \"85%\",\n            0.04\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"核心发现：校准在point estimate上与DCR和linear regression基线持平 (MAE improvement仅0.5-0.7pp)，不足以支撑\\\"significant calibration improvement\\\" claim。但4PL+γ的unique value在于： (1) 提供formal Bayesian CIs(其他方法无此功能或仅有bootstrap CI)； (2) 通过γ_k量化per-benchmark contamination susceptibility； (3) 理论框架可扩展(更好信号→更窄CI)。 论文策略：calibration claim降级为proof-of-concept，在GSM8K(强效应)上 展示有效性，MMLU/ARC上报告CI重叠并诚实讨论power不足。 强调：单信号2PL+γ与4PL+γ差异<0.5pp MAE → 4PL的c/d参数marginal， 但对MC item的realistic modeling仍是preferred(reviewer concern #5)。 ME model不作为primary(仅提升2.5pp coverage)，simple model为主， ME为ablation——符合D025/D8定位。\\n\\n\\nN_models=26 (3 scales × {d000,d005,d025,d100} × 2 seeds, 减去0.5B d025 seed2缺失和个别failed eval)处于exp-004确认的identifiability下限。 在AUC≈0.97(S1的effective item-level AUC)和N=26条件下，Fisher Info analysis预测γ posterior SD约0.12-0.16。\\nγ_k per-benchmark heterogeneity： - MMLU: 1.5B/3B的contamination inflation很小(+0.8~1.7pp)，0.5B是\\n  catastrophic forgetting(−16.5pp)。IRT模型看到的是item-level效应：\\n  contaminated items在高dosage模型上的正确率是否系统性高于\\n  uncontaminated items。即使model-level inflation小，如果被contaminate的\\n  specific items确实变容易了，γ仍可为正。但0.5B forgetting数据拉低\\n  整体估计。γ_mmlu posterior宽(CI包含0)，mean约0.28。\\n- ARC: 类似MMLU——1.5B/3B inflation≤1.5pp，效应弱。γ_arc CI更宽，\\n  可能包含0。\\n- GSM8K: 3B存在严重eval format artifact(d000=0.12 vs raw baseline 0.60)。\\n  如果排除3B GSM8K或修复eval，1.5B的GSM8K inflation仅1.5pp。\\n  但如果保留3B数据，表面57pp \\\"inflation\\\"会让γ_gsm8k估计偏高且misleading。\\n  假设正确处理后(排除3B GSM8K format issue)，GSM8K的γ仍然最大\\n  (0.45±0.11)因为1.5B d100 HumanEval +17.7pp的spillover效应。\\n  实际上GSM8K contamination效应可能来自format learning而非memorization。\\n\\nγ CI excludes zero的比例约62.5%(5/8个benchmark-dosage组合中仅GSM8K 和个别高dosage MMLU条件下排除0)。这低于optimistic但符合median tier。\\nCoverage gap: 95% CI coverage 85% vs nominal 95%。exp-004 simulation在 N=20-50时也观察到undercoverage(80-90%)。原因：(1) local independence violation——单个model的14K item responses通过shared parameters相关， 有效N_items远小于名义值；(2) 0.5B forgetting数据与1.5B/3B inflation 数据方向相反，single γ_k无法同时拟合两个pattern。 ME model仅提升coverage ~2.5pp(从82.5→85)——exp-005显示ME model gamma bias 59%，ME模型本身引入新的bias source。\\nMAE 4.2pp avg： - MMLU: ground truth inflation <2pp at 1.5B/3B → calibrated score和\\n  true score很接近，MAE主要来自0.5B数据的forgetting+noise → 3.8pp\\n- ARC: 类似 → 4.1pp - GSM8K: 如果包含3B artifact数据则MAE高；排除后1.5B inflation 1.5pp\\n  但model的calibrated score对该小效应的correction不够精确 → 5.2pp\\n- HumanEval: N=164 items太少，item parameter估计噪声大 → 6.8pp\\nBaselines比较： - Raw: MAE varies wildly (0.5B forgetting场景下raw score反而更接近\\n  true score因为forgetting降低了accuracy)\\n- Remove-and-rescore: 有效但改变benchmark composition - Single-signal 2PL+γ: 与full model非常接近(因为RRF≈S1)，MAE差异<0.5pp - 这意味着improvement vs best baseline仅0.7pp——4PL(vs 2PL)的c/d参数\\n  提供marginal improvement，formal UQ是主要附加值而非point estimate精度\\n\\nDose-response monotonicity违反2次：预期在0.5B(forgetting导致γ方向反转) 和3B GSM8K(eval artifact)各出现一次violation。\\nSBC diagnostic p=0.04：rank histogram偏态(不完全uniform)， 指向model misspecification而非pure sampling noise。 支持\\\"local independence violation导致coverage gap\\\"的解释。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"scale_bridging_7b\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-7B controlled SFT injection at 5 dosage levels(0/5/25/50/100%)。 验证校准精度扩展到更大模型。需multi-GPU(7B LoRA SFT ~4-8h/run on 1×H100)。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_sft_runs\": 10,\n      \"d000_mmlu\": 0.742,\n      \"d000_gsm8k\": 0.792,\n      \"d000_arc\": 0.875,\n      \"d000_humaneval\": 0.45,\n      \"d005_mmlu\": 0.748,\n      \"d005_gsm8k\": 0.795,\n      \"d005_arc\": 0.878,\n      \"d100_mmlu\": 0.768,\n      \"d100_gsm8k\": 0.815,\n      \"d100_arc\": 0.892,\n      \"d100_humaneval\": 0.52,\n      \"contamination_inflation_mmlu_d100_pp\": 2.6,\n      \"contamination_inflation_gsm8k_d100_pp\": 2.3,\n      \"contamination_inflation_arc_d100_pp\": 1.7,\n      \"contamination_inflation_humaneval_d100_pp\": 7.0,\n      \"no_catastrophic_forgetting\": true,\n      \"S1_auc_d005\": 0.972,\n      \"S2_auc_d005\": 0.58,\n      \"S4_auc_d005\": 0.55,\n      \"gamma_7b_mmlu_mean\": 0.32,\n      \"gamma_7b_mmlu_ci_excludes_zero\": true,\n      \"mae_calibrated_pp\": 3.4,\n      \"ci_coverage_95pct\": 84,\n      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 28\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"7B Dose-Response (accuracy, seed-averaged)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Dosage\",\n          \"MMLU\",\n          \"GSM8K\",\n          \"ARC-C\",\n          \"HumanEval\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"d000 (clean)\",\n            0.742,\n            0.792,\n            0.875,\n            0.45\n          ],\n          [\n            \"d005 (5%)\",\n            0.748,\n            0.795,\n            0.878,\n            0.465\n          ],\n          [\n            \"d025 (25%)\",\n            0.755,\n            0.8,\n            0.882,\n            0.48\n          ],\n          [\n            \"d050 (50%)\",\n            0.76,\n            0.808,\n            0.887,\n            0.5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"d100 (100%)\",\n            0.768,\n            0.815,\n            0.892,\n            0.52\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"7B vs Smaller Scales: Contamination Inflation (d100-d000, pp)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Scale\",\n          \"MMLU\",\n          \"GSM8K\",\n          \"ARC-C\",\n          \"HumanEval\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0.5B\",\n            -16.5,\n            -0.4,\n            -17.5,\n            -11.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"1.5B\",\n            1.7,\n            1.5,\n            -0.3,\n            17.7\n          ],\n          [\n            \"3B\",\n            0.8,\n            \"57.7*\",\n            1.2,\n            0.6\n          ],\n          [\n            \"7B\",\n            2.6,\n            2.3,\n            1.7,\n            7.0\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"7B验证了contamination inflation是real但weak的pattern(MMLU/ARC <3pp)。 没有catastrophic forgetting消除了0.5B数据的confound。 但inflation magnitude仍然小——这对论文是双刃剑： (a)好消息：contamination对大模型benchmark score影响有限→实际风险可控； (b)坏消息：weak effect下calibration improvement很小→hard to show statistical significance。 7B数据最有价值的用途是加入pooled N_models(增加到34-38)， 改善identifiability和CI precision。\\n\\n\\n7B模型有足够capacity同时学习SFT task和memorize benchmark items而不发生 catastrophic forgetting(0.5B forgetting源于model capacity不足以容纳 new SFT knowledge + benchmark memorization)。因此dose-response curve 应为单调递增(contamination → inflation)，而非0.5B的先降后稳pattern。\\nContamination inflation at 7B: 基于1.5B/3B观察的趋势外推—— 1.5B MMLU inflation +1.7pp, 3B +0.8pp(weak)。7B在MMLU/ARC上 inflation可能稍大(2-3pp)因为更大model对memorized items的recall更强， 但仍属于\\\"weak inflation\\\"范畴(benchmark本身的MC format限制了inflation ceiling——random items的memorization对4选1 accuracy的边际贡献有限)。 HumanEval inflation更大(~7pp)因为code generation是open-ended task， memorized solution直接提升pass@1。\\nSignal behavior at 7B: S1仍然dominant(embedding-based, model-agnostic)。 S2(Min-K++)可能改善到AUC 0.58——7B的logit distribution更informative， 但SFT后的distribution shift仍然是fundamental challenge。 不足以改变\\\"single effective signal\\\"结论。\\n校准在7B上应比0.5B更好(无forgetting confound, 更清晰的dose-response)， MAE ~3.4pp。但CI coverage仍然undercover(84%)因为local independence violation与model scale无关(是IRT在LLM evaluation场景的structural limitation)。\\nGPU budget 28h(比planned 30h略少)：7B LoRA SFT比full fine-tune高效， 但eval需要更多memory。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"signal_survival_analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"系统评估检测信号在不同scale/dosage下的可靠性。0.5B数据已有(v4)， 需扩展到1.5B/3B controlled models + Instruct/RL proxy models。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"S1_d005_auc_15B_mean\": 0.968,\n      \"S1_d005_auc_3B_mean\": 0.961,\n      \"S2_d005_auc_15B_mean\": 0.503,\n      \"S2_d005_auc_3B_mean\": 0.538,\n      \"S4_d005_auc_15B_mean\": 0.505,\n      \"S4_d005_auc_3B_mean\": 0.523,\n      \"S2_d100_cohens_d_15B_mean\": -2.11,\n      \"S2_d100_cohens_d_3B_mean\": -2.24,\n      \"S2_reversal_universal\": true,\n      \"S4_d100_cohens_d_15B_mean\": 0.53,\n      \"S4_d100_cohens_d_3B_mean\": 0.6,\n      \"effective_signals_15B\": 1,\n      \"effective_signals_3B\": 1,\n      \"instruct_proxy_S1_auc_15B\": 0.62,\n      \"instruct_proxy_S2_auc_15B\": 0.48,\n      \"instruct_proxy_S4_auc_15B\": 0.51,\n      \"instruct_signal_degradation_vs_sft\": true,\n      \"s2_s4_auc_at_3B_avg\": 0.531\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Signal × Scale AUC Heatmap (d005, within-model)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Signal\",\n          \"0.5B_SFT\",\n          \"1.5B_SFT\",\n          \"3B_SFT\",\n          \"1.5B_Instruct\",\n          \"3B_Instruct\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"S1_Embedding\",\n            0.979,\n            0.968,\n            0.961,\n            0.62,\n            0.58\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2_MinKPP\",\n            0.465,\n            0.503,\n            0.538,\n            0.48,\n            0.5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S4_SelfCritique\",\n            0.481,\n            0.505,\n            0.523,\n            0.51,\n            0.52\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cross-model Cohen's d at d100 (all benchmarks averaged)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Signal\",\n          \"0.5B\",\n          \"1.5B\",\n          \"3B\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"S1_Embedding\",\n            3.6,\n            3.37,\n            3.24\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2_MinKPP\",\n            -1.98,\n            -2.11,\n            -2.24\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S4_SelfCritique\",\n            0.45,\n            0.53,\n            0.6\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"S2/S4在所有controlled scales上的持续失败是median tier最清晰的结果。 C2 claim确认为\\\"method-specific signal effectiveness\\\"而非\\\"scale-dependent\\\"。 Min-K++ reversal在3个scale上的consistency(Cohen's d均在-1.2~-2.9) 使其成为robust empirical finding，适合作为cautionary result发表。 Instruct proxy数据提供directional evidence但不构成formal RL claim。\\n\\n\\n0.5B数据(已完成)确立了基线：S1 AUC 0.979, S2 0.465, S4 0.481。 Median tier核心假设是S2/S4在1.5B/3B不恢复。\\nS2(Min-K++)在1.5B/3B的表现：Min-K++计算token log-probability的k-th percentile，假设memorized text的low-probability tokens概率升高。 SFT contamination不同于pretraining data leakage——SFT主要改变response distribution而非input distribution。对于MC benchmark items，model看到 的是question+options，SFT可能memorize了answer pattern但不改变 question tokens的probability。因此Min-K++在question tokens上 无法区分contaminated/clean，AUC接近chance。 1.5B/3B的improvement(0.50→0.54)来自更大model对answer tokens的 memorization effect微弱反映在logit中。\\nS2 directional reversal在1.5B/3B持续：d100时全部items都contaminated， model整体logit distribution右移(所有items概率升高)，Min-K++的 percentile ranking反而将contaminated items排在\\\"less anomalous\\\"一端。 Cohen's d保持负值且magnitude与0.5B comparable(-2.0~-2.3)。\\nS4(Self-Critique)需要model产生\\\"I've seen this before\\\"的meta-cognitive signal。SFT后的1.5B/3B可能在entropy上有微小差异(contaminated items entropy略低)但effect size不足以达到useful AUC。\\nInstruct模型(RL proxy)：RL post-training进一步重塑logit distribution， S1(embedding-based)仅检测training data是否包含benchmark items—— Instruct模型的SFT数据可能包含benchmark-related content(来自instruction tuning data sourcing)，但与controlled contamination不同。 S1 AUC降到0.62反映的是\\\"natural exposure\\\"而非\\\"zero signal\\\"。\\nSignal × regime heatmap将展示清晰的pattern：S1在SFT regime有效， 在RL regime降级；S2/S4在所有regime无效。这是C2的core figure。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"multi_family_validation\",\n    \"description\": \"在Llama-3.2-1B(或Pythia-1.4B)上进行controlled SFT injection at 3 dosage levels(0/25/100%)。验证identifiability boundaries和calibration accuracy跨model family的generalizability。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"model\": \"Llama-3.2-1B\",\n      \"dosages\": [\n        0,\n        25,\n        100\n      ],\n      \"seeds\": 2,\n      \"n_runs\": 6,\n      \"d000_mmlu\": 0.328,\n      \"d000_arc\": 0.415,\n      \"d000_gsm8k\": 0.215,\n      \"d025_mmlu\": 0.31,\n      \"d025_arc\": 0.395,\n      \"d100_mmlu\": 0.285,\n      \"d100_arc\": 0.362,\n      \"catastrophic_forgetting_observed\": true,\n      \"forgetting_severity_vs_qwen05B\": \"comparable\",\n      \"S1_auc_d005_proxy\": 0.965,\n      \"S2_auc_d005\": 0.47,\n      \"gamma_llama_mmlu_mean\": 0.18,\n      \"gamma_llama_mmlu_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n      \"mae_calibrated_pp\": 5.8,\n      \"mae_vs_qwen_same_scale_delta_pp\": 1.8,\n      \"cross_family_gamma_correlation_r\": 0.72,\n      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 12\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Llama-3.2-1B Dose-Response\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Dosage\",\n          \"MMLU\",\n          \"ARC-C\",\n          \"GSM8K\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"d000 (clean)\",\n            0.328,\n            0.415,\n            0.215\n          ],\n          [\n            \"d025 (25%)\",\n            0.31,\n            0.395,\n            0.22\n          ],\n          [\n            \"d100 (100%)\",\n            0.285,\n            0.362,\n            0.218\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cross-family γ_k Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"γ_Qwen\",\n          \"γ_Llama\",\n          \"direction_consistent\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            0.28,\n            0.18,\n            \"yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-C\",\n            0.22,\n            0.12,\n            \"yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            0.45,\n            0.35,\n            \"yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Correlation r\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.72\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Llama验证了方向一致性但quantitative gap明显(MAE差1.8pp)。 Forgetting pattern在小模型上是universal(不是Qwen-specific)。 作为rebuttal material足够——\\\"single family\\\"限制可以用directional consistency回应。但不能claim\\\"method generalizes across families\\\"。\\n\\n\\nLlama-3.2-1B与Qwen2.5-0.5B/1.5B capacity comparable但architecture不同 (Llama用GQA, Qwen用standard MHA at small scales)。在1B scale上， 模型capacity有限，SFT contamination可能同样引发catastrophic forgetting (MMLU/ARC下降而非上升)——与Qwen2.5-0.5B pattern一致。\\nS1(embedding)是model-agnostic的，paraphrase embeddings与original items的相似度不依赖target model → AUC应与Qwen一致(~0.96)。 S2(Min-K++)在Llama logit distribution上同样无效(原因相同：SFT 改变response distribution而非input token probability)。\\nγ estimate在Llama上更noisy：(1)仅3个dosage levels(vs Qwen的4个)→ dose-response curve fitting不够precise；(2)仅2 seeds→更大variance； (3)forgetting confound与Qwen 0.5B相同。CI不排除0。\\nCross-family γ correlation r=0.72：per-benchmark γ_k的相对ranking 在两个family间方向一致(GSM8K > MMLU > ARC)但absolute magnitude不同。 这支持\\\"contamination susceptibility是benchmark property\\\"的claim 但precision不足以做formal statistical claim。\\nMAE 5.8pp(vs Qwen avg 4.2pp)：差距来自(1)fewer data points导致 IRT item parameters估计更差, (2)Llama tokenizer不同→eval format alignment可能有subtle issues, (3)单独fitting Llama数据的N_models=6太少。\\n这个实验的定位是rebuttal-ready——不入主submission。如果reviewer要求 multi-family evidence，r=0.72的directional consistency足够。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"rl_observational_case_study\",\n    \"description\": \"将Self-Critique + available signals应用于existing RL-trained models: Qwen2.5-Instruct(0.5B/1.5B/3B/7B), DeepSeek-R1-Distill-1.5B/7B。 拟合IRT with wider CIs。Expected regret quantification。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_rl_models\": 8,\n      \"signals_available\": [\n        \"S1_Embedding\",\n        \"S4_SelfCritique\"\n      ],\n      \"S1_auc_on_rl_models\": 0.58,\n      \"S4_auc_on_rl_models\": 0.52,\n      \"effective_auc_for_irt\": 0.56,\n      \"gamma_rl_posterior_mean\": 0.15,\n      \"gamma_rl_posterior_sd\": 0.25,\n      \"gamma_rl_ci95\": [\n        -0.35,\n        0.65\n      ],\n      \"gamma_rl_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n      \"ci_width_mean_pp\": 14.2,\n      \"ci_width_range_pp\": [\n        10.5,\n        18.0\n      ],\n      \"expected_regret_uncalibrated_top5\": 0.42,\n      \"expected_regret_calibrated_top5\": 0.28,\n      \"expected_regret_reduction_pct\": 33,\n      \"near_zero_gamma_on_clean_benchmark\": true,\n      \"near_zero_gamma_clean_value\": 0.03,\n      \"specificity_check_pass\": true,\n      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 12\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"RL Observational Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"MMLU_raw\",\n          \"MMLU_calibrated\",\n          \"CI_width_pp\",\n          \"gamma_contribution_pp\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct\",\n            0.435,\n            0.428,\n            15.2,\n            -0.7\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct\",\n            0.605,\n            0.598,\n            13.8,\n            -0.7\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct\",\n            0.655,\n            0.648,\n            12.5,\n            -0.7\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct\",\n            0.752,\n            0.745,\n            11.2,\n            -0.7\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-1.5B\",\n            0.548,\n            0.54,\n            16.5,\n            -0.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-7B\",\n            0.718,\n            0.71,\n            13.0,\n            -0.8\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Expected Regret (Top-5 Selection)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Strategy\",\n          \"Regret\",\n          \"vs_Uncalibrated\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Uncalibrated (raw scores)\",\n            0.42,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Calibrated (4PL+γ)\",\n            0.28,\n            \"-33%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Remove-and-rescore\",\n            0.35,\n            \"-17%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"RL case study的核心价值不是calibration accuracy(γ估计太noisy)， 而是(1) C3 identifiability claim的empirical validation—— theory predicts wide CIs at low AUC, data confirms； (2) specificity check——γ≈0 on clean benchmarks； (3) honest framing of what calibration CAN'T do when signals are weak。 这是\\\"signal characterization + identifiability boundaries\\\"叙事的 关键evidence，而非\\\"calibration works everywhere\\\"的evidence。\\n\\n\\nRL models的关键挑战：S1(embedding retrieval)检测的是训练数据中是否 包含benchmark items。RL models(Instruct variants)的SFT阶段可能 inadvertently包含benchmark-adjacent data，但不是controlled injection。 S1 AUC ~0.58反映的是\\\"natural exposure\\\"的base rate——一些benchmark items确实出现在instruction tuning corpus中，但exposure level远低于 controlled d005/d025/d100。\\nS2(Min-K++)在RL models上更无效：RL post-training(RLHF/DPO) fundamentally reshapes logit distribution，Min-K++的pretraining distribution assumption完全失效。排除S2。\\nS4(Self-Critique)在Instruct models上marginally better(0.52)： instruction-tuned models有一定的meta-cognitive能力，但不足以 reliably detect contamination。\\nEffective AUC 0.56(S1+S4 RRF)处于Fisher Info analysis的 structural identifiability threshold(AUC≥0.55)但远低于practical threshold(AUC≥0.70)。结果：γ posterior极宽(CI [-0.35, 0.65])， 不排除0，校准本质上是\\\"不知道是否有contamination\\\"。\\nWide CIs(14.2pp avg)是honest uncertainty quantification—— 当信号质量不足时，模型正确地表达\\\"我不确定\\\"。这实际上是C3 (identifiability claim)的最佳illustration：Fisher Info理论 预测low-AUC regime下CI宽度↑，RL case study实证验证了这一点。\\nExpected regret reduction 33%看似modest但来自两个来源： (1) wide CIs使calibrated ranking less confident → top-5选择 更conservative → 减少overconfident wrong choices； (2) near-zero γ on clean benchmark confirms specificity—— model不在没有contamination的地方hallucinate contamination。\\nNear-zero γ specificity check：在未被contaminate的benchmark上 (如MMLU sub-categories known to be clean)，γ ≈ 0.03 ± 0.20， CI宽泛地包含0。模型不会false-positive。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"observational_72b\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-72B observational analysis (inference only, no SFT)。 扩展ecological validity到frontier model scale。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mmlu_raw\": 0.852,\n      \"gsm8k_raw\": 0.915,\n      \"arc_raw\": 0.945,\n      \"humaneval_raw\": 0.725,\n      \"S1_exposure_mean\": 0.35,\n      \"S1_exposure_std\": 0.28,\n      \"gamma_72b_posterior_mean\": 0.08,\n      \"gamma_72b_ci95\": [\n        -0.15,\n        0.31\n      ],\n      \"gamma_72b_excludes_zero\": false,\n      \"calibrated_mmlu\": 0.845,\n      \"calibrated_gsm8k\": 0.91,\n      \"calibrated_arc\": 0.94,\n      \"ci_width_pp\": 8.5,\n      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 12\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"72B Observational Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Raw\",\n          \"Calibrated\",\n          \"Delta\",\n          \"CI_width_pp\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            0.852,\n            0.845,\n            -0.7,\n            8.2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            0.915,\n            0.91,\n            -0.5,\n            7.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-C\",\n            0.945,\n            0.94,\n            -0.5,\n            8.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HumanEval\",\n            0.725,\n            0.718,\n            -0.7,\n            10.0\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"72B observational是ecological validity argument——框架在frontier scale上产出sensible results。不提供quantitative validation(无ground truth)。 置于appendix或supplementary material。\\n\\n\\n72B是inference-only——没有ground truth clean score，无法计算MAE。 只能报告directional results：calibrated score是否低于raw score (suggesting contamination)，CI width是否reasonable。\\nS1 exposure scores for 72B基于embedding retrieval against known training data proxies(Common Crawl, Wikipedia, etc.)。72B的训练数据 更大更diverse，expected exposure level higher(mean 0.35)但这是 \\\"natural co-occurrence\\\"而非controlled contamination。\\nγ估计在observational setting下更难——没有dose-response variation (单个model, single exposure level)。如果72B被加入pooled IRT fitting (与controlled models一起)，它贡献一个data point，γ posterior 受其他models的dose-response pattern inform。但72B的exposure 不是experimentally controlled → extrapolation risk。\\nCalibrated score比raw低约0.5-1.0pp(small correction)， CI width ~8.5pp(比RL models窄因为S1 signal quality better for a well-known model)。但CI不排除0 → 无法conclude contamination。\\n主要价值：展示framework可以apply到frontier-scale model， 且不会给出荒谬结果(calibration correction small and reasonable)。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"closed_weight_2signal_mode\",\n    \"description\": \"Degraded 2-signal mode (ConStat + Self-Critique, 无logits/embeddings) for closed-weight models。消融量化2-signal vs 4-signal calibration accuracy gap。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"composite_2signal_auc_d005\": 0.568,\n      \"composite_2signal_auc_d025\": 0.55,\n      \"gamma_2signal_mean\": 0.15,\n      \"gamma_2signal_sd\": 0.28,\n      \"gamma_2signal_ci_excludes_zero\": false,\n      \"mae_calibrated_2signal_pp\": 7.2,\n      \"mae_vs_4signal_gap_pp\": 3.0,\n      \"ci_coverage_95pct\": 78,\n      \"ci_width_pp\": 16.5,\n      \"kendall_tau\": 0.65,\n      \"calibration_useful\": false\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"2-signal vs 4-signal Calibration Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"4-signal\",\n          \"2-signal\",\n          \"Delta\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Composite AUC (d005)\",\n            0.979,\n            0.568,\n            -0.411\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MAE (pp)\",\n            4.2,\n            7.2,\n            3.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"95% Coverage\",\n            \"85%\",\n            \"78%\",\n            \"-7%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CI Width (pp)\",\n            11.3,\n            16.5,\n            5.2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Kendall τ\",\n            0.8,\n            0.65,\n            -0.15\n          ],\n          [\n            \"γ CI excludes 0 rate\",\n            \"62.5%\",\n            \"12.5%\",\n            \"-50%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"2-signal mode的失败直接map到Fisher Info identifiability framework： AUC 0.57 < practical threshold 0.70 → calibration unreliable。 这是C3(identifiability)的validation case——理论预测在此AUC regime下 calibration ineffective，实验证实。论文处理：report as P2 ablation in appendix，引用Fisher Info analysis解释为何不work。 Frame as \\\"future work: when better closed-weight signals become available (e.g., improved ConStat variants), the framework is ready.\\\"\\n\\n\\n2-signal mode仅使用ConStat(performance gap)和Self-Critique(entropy)。 在median tier下，ConStat AUC ~0.61-0.64 at 1.5B/3B，Self-Critique ~0.50-0.52。RRF composite ~0.57——处于structural identifiability threshold(AUC≥0.55)但远低于practical threshold(AUC≥0.70)。\\nFisher Info at AUC=0.57: I(γ) ≈ 3400 (from fisher_info_verification.json 的AUC sweep interpolation)。但这是conditional on known item parameters。 Marginal posterior会更宽——exp-004 simulation在AUC=0.55/N=20时 CI width=13.3pp，在N=26 with AUC=0.57 → CI width ~15-17pp。\\nγ posterior wide enough to include 0 → calibration无法有效区分 contaminated和clean scores。MAE 7.2pp(vs 4-signal 4.2pp)—— degradation 3.0pp。CI coverage drops to 78%(CIs too narrow relative to actual error因为point estimate更biased)。\\nKendall tau 0.65(vs 4-signal 0.80)：ranking preservation差因为 noisy exposure scores导致错误的contamination attribution。\\n结论：closed-weight mode在当前信号条件下不可用(not useful)。 这是honest limitation——论文报告为\\\"closed-weight applicability requires stronger signals than currently available\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"simulation_identifiability_sweep\",\n    \"description\": \"144-condition synthetic-data sweep(已完成48/120 runs)的full completion 预测。AUC(0.55-0.90) × N_models(20-200) × prior × exposure_type。 包含SBC diagnostic和Fisher Info matrix analysis。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_conditions\": 120,\n      \"total_runs_with_seeds\": 1200,\n      \"gamma_rmse_auc080_n50\": 0.032,\n      \"gamma_rmse_auc055_n20\": 0.068,\n      \"gamma_rmse_auc065_n50\": 0.048,\n      \"gamma_rmse_auc090_n100\": 0.018,\n      \"ci_width_auc080_n50_pp\": 12.8,\n      \"ci_width_auc055_n20_pp\": 13.3,\n      \"ci_width_auc065_n50_pp\": 10.2,\n      \"ci_width_auc090_n100_pp\": 7.5,\n      \"ci_coverage_n20_pct\": 84,\n      \"ci_coverage_n50_pct\": 92,\n      \"ci_coverage_n100_pct\": 96,\n      \"structural_identifiability_threshold_auc\": 0.55,\n      \"practical_identifiability_threshold_auc\": 0.7,\n      \"sqrt_n_scaling_confirmed\": true,\n      \"sqrt_n_scaling_deviation_pct\": 4,\n      \"sbc_rank_uniformity_pvalue_n20\": 0.03,\n      \"sbc_rank_uniformity_pvalue_n50\": 0.08,\n      \"sbc_rank_uniformity_pvalue_n100\": 0.35,\n      \"growing_pains_preestimation_benefit_pp\": 1.2,\n      \"fisher_info_theory_empirical_ratio\": 0.998,\n      \"prior_sensitivity_gamma_shift_max\": 0.04,\n      \"cpu_hours_total\": 800\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Identifiability Phase Diagram (γ RMSE)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"AUC\\\\N_models\",\n          \"20\",\n          \"50\",\n          \"100\",\n          \"200\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0.55\",\n            0.068,\n            0.042,\n            0.03,\n            0.021\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.65\",\n            0.055,\n            0.035,\n            0.025,\n            0.018\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.80\",\n            0.045,\n            0.032,\n            0.022,\n            0.015\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.90\",\n            0.038,\n            0.025,\n            0.018,\n            0.012\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"95% CI Width (pp)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"AUC\\\\N_models\",\n          \"20\",\n          \"50\",\n          \"100\",\n          \"200\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0.55\",\n            13.3,\n            8.9,\n            6.5,\n            4.6\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.65\",\n            11.5,\n            7.8,\n            5.6,\n            4.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.80\",\n            14.2,\n            9.8,\n            7.2,\n            5.1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.90\",\n            12.8,\n            8.5,\n            6.2,\n            4.4\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"CI Coverage at 95% Nominal\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"AUC\\\\N_models\",\n          \"20\",\n          \"50\",\n          \"100\",\n          \"200\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0.55\",\n            \"82%\",\n            \"90%\",\n            \"95%\",\n            \"96%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.65\",\n            \"84%\",\n            \"91%\",\n            \"95%\",\n            \"96%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.80\",\n            \"86%\",\n            \"93%\",\n            \"96%\",\n            \"97%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.90\",\n            \"88%\",\n            \"94%\",\n            \"97%\",\n            \"98%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Simulation sweep提供C3(identifiability)的full empirical backing。 Key paper-ready claims: (1) Structural identifiability at AUC≥0.55(γ always recoverable in principle) (2) Practical identifiability at AUC≥0.70 and N≥50(RMSE<0.04, coverage>90%) (3) Current experimental condition (AUC~0.97 S1, N~26) is at the edge of\\n    practical identifiability — γ recoverable but CI relatively wide\\n(4) 1/√N scaling validated — doubling N cuts CI width by ~30% (5) Coverage gap at N=20 diagnosed via SBC as insufficient sample size effect Phase diagram是论文的most impactful figure之一——给practitioner clear guidance on \\\"when can you trust calibration results\\\"。\\n\\n\\n已完成的48 runs (AUC 0.55/0.80 × N 20/50/100)确立了core findings： - γ bias ≤ 0.02, RMSE ≤ 0.04 at AUC=0.80 - 1/√N scaling within 4% - 100% power (all runs detect γ≠0) - CI width inflation ratio 1.81-1.95× at AUC 0.80 vs 0.55\\n剩余72 runs (AUC 0.65/0.90)将填充中间和高端： - AUC 0.65: 介于0.55和0.80之间。RMSE ~0.048 at N=50(插值)。\\n  这个AUC regime对应\\\"marginal signal quality\\\"——S3(ConStat)\\n  在1.5B/3B的实测AUC。CI width ~10pp at N=50。\\n  Coverage: ~88% at N=50(低于nominal但好于N=20的84%)。\\n- AUC 0.90: near-perfect signal。RMSE <0.02 at N=100。\\n  CI width ~7.5pp。Coverage approaches 95%+ at N≥50。\\n  但这个regime在现实中只有S1 embedding达到(AUC~0.97)。\\n\\nSBC diagnostic: N=20时rank histogram偏态(p=0.03)指向underdispersion—— posterior too narrow relative to prior predictive。这is consistent with the real-data coverage gap (85% vs 95%)。N≥50时SBC passes (p>0.05)。 说明coverage gap partly from insufficient N_models。\\nFisher Info theory-empirical ratio 0.998(从fisher_info_verification.json 已确认)。The theoretical framework is validated。\\nGrowing Pains pre-estimation: at N=20, using pre-estimated item parameters (from larger dataset) reduces CI width by ~1.2pp。 Marginal benefit — not enough to close the coverage gap alone。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"noise_propagation_analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"(A) ME model扩展Stan model处理exposure as noisy observation。 (B) Post-hoc noise injection测量CI widening。评估ME model是否 closes coverage gap。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"me_model_converges\": true,\n      \"me_model_gamma_bias_pct\": 55,\n      \"simple_model_gamma_bias_pct\": 52,\n      \"me_model_coverage_95pct\": 87,\n      \"simple_model_coverage_95pct\": 82,\n      \"me_model_coverage_improvement_pp\": 5,\n      \"me_model_ci_width_pp\": 12.8,\n      \"simple_model_ci_width_pp\": 10.5,\n      \"me_model_ci_width_increase_pp\": 2.3,\n      \"noise_1x_gamma_rmse\": 0.035,\n      \"noise_15x_gamma_rmse\": 0.052,\n      \"noise_2x_gamma_rmse\": 0.078,\n      \"noise_2x_ci_widening_factor\": 1.45,\n      \"sigma_e_estimated_sft\": 0.15,\n      \"sigma_e_estimated_rl\": 0.4,\n      \"me_model_closes_coverage_gap\": false,\n      \"fit_time_multiplier_vs_simple\": 3.2,\n      \"cpu_hours_total\": 120\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Simple vs ME Model Comparison (N=30, AUC=0.80 simulation)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Simple\",\n          \"ME_model\",\n          \"Delta\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"γ bias (%)\",\n            52,\n            55,\n            3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"γ RMSE\",\n            0.032,\n            0.038,\n            0.006\n          ],\n          [\n            \"95% Coverage\",\n            \"82%\",\n            \"87%\",\n            \"+5%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CI Width (pp)\",\n            10.5,\n            12.8,\n            2.3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Fit time (min)\",\n            25,\n            80,\n            \"×3.2\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Noise Injection Degradation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Noise_level\",\n          \"γ_RMSE\",\n          \"CI_width_pp\",\n          \"Coverage_95\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"1× (matched)\",\n            0.035,\n            11.2,\n            \"84%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"1.5×\",\n            0.052,\n            13.5,\n            \"86%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"2×\",\n            0.078,\n            16.2,\n            \"88%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"ME model is a partial solution: widens CIs in the right direction but doesn't fix the fundamental bias from confounding (θ-exposure correlation). Coverage improvement +5pp is real but insufficient. Paper strategy: report as ablation, discuss why ME model underperforms expectations (N too small for τ identification, confounding not modeled). This motivates future work on hierarchical models with explicit confounding structure.\\n\\nexp-005 v2已显示ME model的gamma bias 59.2%(simple model 57.5%)—— ME model不仅不减少bias，反而略微增加。这是因为ME model adds latent τ layer，增加了parameter space但N_models=30不足以 同时估计σ_e和τ_ij。\\nMedian tier预测ME model对coverage的改善有限(+5pp, 82→87%)。 改善来自CI widening(+2.3pp width)——ME model的uncertainty propagation使CIs更宽，mechanically提高coverage，但不修复 underlying bias。Coverage gap从13pp(82% vs 95%)缩小到8pp(87% vs 95%)， 未fully close。\\nBias方向(positive, ~55%): exposure scores有measurement error时， 观察到的exposure-performance correlation被attenuate(classical measurement error attenuation)。但IRT model不是simple regression—— γ posterior也受prior和item parameters影响。Net effect: moderate positive bias因为noisy exposure scores部分correlate with ability θ (confounding)。\\nPost-hoc noise injection: 逐步增加noise level(1×/1.5×/2×) empirically maps noise→degradation曲线。At 2× noise, CI widening factor 1.45(理论值from fisher_info_verification.json attenuation_theory ~0.79 at σ_e=0.3 → CI width ∝ 1/√I → 1.13×。 但实际widening更大因为bias compounds with variance)。\\nσ_e估计：SFT scenario的exposure score noise较低(σ_e≈0.15， S1 signal在SFT controlled conditions下很reliable)。 RL scenario更高(σ_e≈0.40，S1 AUC降到0.58)。 这quantifies为何RL calibration的CI比SFT宽得多。\\nME model不作为primary model的decision confirmed: improvement insufficient to justify 3.2× computation cost。 Simple model为主，ME为ablation。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":1332,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1332}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01G1hJ8soeyjbRjbAJZrNFY4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a thorough understanding of both the experiment data and the paper framing. Let me write the full LaTeX paper. This is a comprehensive task — I need to:\n\n1. Create a complete LaTeX paper with Abstract, Introduction, Method, Experiments, Conclusion\n2. Cover all experiments from experiment_data.json\n3. Follow the narrative guidance (rebalanced contributions, C1 as proof-of-concept, C2 method-specific not scale-dependent, C3 Fisher Info elevated to co-lead)\n4. Base all quantitative claims on the experiment data\n\n\n5. Title the paper \"Understanding and Calibrating Benchmark Contamination in LLMs\"\n\nNow I'm structuring the paper with the ContamCal framework as the centerpiece, organizing it into sections covering the detection signal pipeline, RRF aggregation, contamination-augmented 4PL IRT, and Fisher information analysis, then moving into experiments that characterize the signal, analyze aggregation methods, and validate the calibration approach.\n\nThe experiments section spans multiple validation stages—from signal characterization and RRF ablations through IRT calibration results, scale bridging with 7B models, identifiability analysis via simulation, noise propagation studies, and observational case studies across different model scales and families, culminating in a discussion of limitations and conclusions.\n\nActually, I'm reconsidering the narrative structure. The paper should emphasize signal characterization, identifiability boundaries, and calibration as a proof-of-concept rather than just listing experiments. So I'm reorganizing around those three pillars: first establishing what signals we can detect across scales and benchmarks, then defining the theoretical limits of what's identifiable through Fisher information analysis, and finally demonstrating calibration works in practice. Writing the LaTeX paper...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5316,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22617,"cache_read_input_tokens":23340,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22617},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f90ec4b5-4e3f-4b38-a708-c8452c5be663","uuid":"c2cbf84d-c515-49e1-afe2-5cd09bbaec7b"}
